  {
    "global index": "GeoBench_1123",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After decades of Soviet rule and control of Eastern Europe, in 1989, the Berlin Wall and the Iron Curtain fell, precipitating the end of the Soviet Union. This is best described as an example of which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Devolution\nB. Heartland theory\nC. Imperialism\nD. Balkanization\nE. Annexation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**. \n\n**Devolution** refers to the transition of power from a central government to regional or local levels, or the complete breakup of a state into smaller independent units, as seen with the collapse of the Soviet Union. While \"Balkanization\" describes a violent fragmentation into mutually hostile states, the broader geopolitical process of the USSR’s dissolution is most accurately categorized as devolution. The other options, such as Heartland theory (a geopolitical strategy) or Imperialism (extension of power), do not describe the act of a state breaking apart.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
