    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Carl Sauer would most strongly agree with which of the following statements?\n\nOptions: \nA. Environmental determinism means humans possess the skills necessary to modify their environment to fit their needs.\nB. Environmental determinism is both factually incorrect and a prejudicial tool of Western colonialism.\nC. Neo-environmental determinism means humans possess the skills necessary to modify their environment to fit their needs.\nD. Neo-environmental determinism is both factually incorrect and a prejudicial tool of Western colonialism.\nE. The possibilist approach to geographic study concludes that cultures are a direct result of where they exist.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
