    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nFor an average American who hasn't visited the area, \"Western Europe\" is a **perceptual region** (or vernacular region) because it is defined by subjective cultural, historical, and political perceptions rather than strict physical borders. While it has geographic and economic components, the mental \"image\" of what countries belong there varies based on individual stereotypes and associations. This contrasts with formal functional or geographic regions that rely on precise data or physical features.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
