      "generated_answer": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we first rewrite \\(\\sec x\\) in terms of cosine:\n\\[ \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\sin x \\cos x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}. \\]\nNext, we find a common denominator, which is \\(\\sin x \\cos x\\), and subtract:\n\\[ \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}. \\]\nUsing the definition of the cotangent function, \\(\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x\\).\n\n\\boxed{\\cot x}",
