    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $F(z)=\\frac{{z+i}}{{z-i}}$ for all complex numbers $z\\not= i,$ and let $z_n=F(z_{{n-1}})$ for all positive integers $n.$ Given that $z_0=\\frac 1{{137}}+i,$ find $z_{{2002}}.$\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $z_{2002}$, we first examine the behavior of the function $F(z) = \\frac{z+i}{z-i}$.\nCalculating the first few iterations:\n$z_1 = F(z_0) = \\frac{z_0+i}{z_0-i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137}+2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i$\n$z_2 = F(z_1) = \\frac{(1+274i)+i}{(1+274i)-i} = \\frac{1+275i}{1+273i}$\n$z_3 = F(z_2) = \\frac{\\frac{1+275i}{1+273i}+i}{\\frac{1+275i}{1+273i}-i} = \\frac{1+275i+i-273}{1+275i-i+273} = \\frac{-272+276i}{274+274i} = \\frac{-136+138i}{137+137i}$\nActually, it is more efficient to look for a cycle or a trigonometric substitution. Let $z = i \\cot \\theta$. Then $F(i \\cot \\theta) = \\frac{i \\cot \\theta + i}{i \\cot \\theta - i} = \\frac{\\cot \\theta + 1}{\\cot \\theta - 1} = \\cot(\\theta - \\frac{\\pi}{4})$.\nApplying $F$ $n$ times yields $z_n = i \\cot(\\theta_0 - \\frac{n\\pi}{4})$.\nFor $z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i$, we have $i \\cot \\theta_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\implies \\cot \\theta_0 = 1 - \\frac{i}{137}$.\n$z_{2002} = i \\cot(\\theta_0 - \\frac{2002\\pi}{4}) = i \\cot(\\theta_0 - 500\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2}) = i \\tan \\theta_0$.\nSince $\\cot \\theta_0 = 1 - \\frac{i}{137} = \\frac{137-i}{137}$, we have $\\tan \\theta_0 = \\frac{137}{137-i} = \\frac{137(137+i)}{137^2+1} = \\frac{137(137+i)}{18770}$.\nThus $z_{2002} = i \\frac{137(137+i)}{18770} = \\frac{137(137i-1)}{18770} = \\frac{137i-1}{137} = i - \\frac{1}{137}$.\n\n\\boxed{i - \\frac{1}{137}}",
