    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of $b,$ we first identify two points on the line from the provided grid. Looking at the graph, the line passes through the points $(-5, 4)$ and $(-1, 3).$\n\nThe direction vector of the line can be found by calculating the difference between these two points:\n$$\\vec{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 - (-5) \\\\ 3 - 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}$$\nAny scalar multiple of this vector is also a direction vector for the line. We are given that the direction vector is of the form $\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix},$ so we set up the proportion:\n$$\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot k = \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}$$\nSolving for $k$ using the first component: $4k = -7 \\implies k = -\\frac{7}{4}.$ \nNow, solve for $b$ using the second component: $b = -1 \\cdot k = -1 \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{7}{4}\\right) = \\frac{7}{4}.$\n\n\\boxed{7/4}",
