    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the height $h$ of the cylinder, we use the formula for the volume of a cylinder, which is $V = \\pi r^2 h$. \n\nGiven that the radius $r = 3$ cm and the volume $V = 45\\pi$ cubic cm, we substitute these values into the formula:\n$$45\\pi = \\pi (3)^2 h$$\n$$45\\pi = 9\\pi h$$\n\nDividing both sides by $9\\pi$, we get:\n$$h = \\frac{45\\pi}{9\\pi} = 5$$\n\nThe height of the cylinder is 5 cm.\n\n\\boxed{5}",
