    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In $\\triangle RST$, the angle at $S$ is a right angle ($90^\\circ$), making it a right triangle where the hypotenuse $RT = 5$. Since $\\sin R = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\frac{ST}{RT} = \\frac{2}{5}$, we find that the length of side $ST$ is $2$. Using the Pythagorean theorem for $\\triangle RST$, we find $RS = \\sqrt{RT^2 - ST^2} = \\sqrt{5^2 - 2^2} = \\sqrt{21}$. Finally, we calculate $\\sin T = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\frac{RS}{RT} = \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}$.\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}}",
