      "generated_answer": "To find the range of $y = \\log_2(\\sqrt{\\sin x})$ for $0^\\circ < x < 180^\\circ$, we first determine the range of the inner function $\\sin x$. For $0^\\circ < x < 180^\\circ$, the value of $\\sin x$ spans the interval $(0, 1]$.\n\nNext, we calculate the range of $\\sqrt{\\sin x}$, which is $(0, 1]$. Applying the base-2 logarithm to this interval, since $\\log_2(u)$ is a strictly increasing function, the range becomes $(\\lim_{u \\to 0^+} \\log_2 u, \\log_2 1]$, which simplifies to $(-\\infty, 0]$.\n\nThus, the range of the function is the set of all real numbers less than or equal to 0.\n\n\\boxed{(-\\infty, 0]}",
