      "generated_answer": "To find the set of vectors $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix}$ such that their projection onto $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ is the zero vector, we use the formula for projection:\n\\[\\operatorname{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2} \\mathbf{a}.\\]\nSince $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$, the projection is the zero vector if and only if the dot product $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 0$. This gives the equation $2x + 1y = 0$, which simplifies to $y = -2x$.\n\n\\boxed{y = -2x}",
