      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. Operator**.\n\nIn genetics, an **operator** is a short sequence of DNA located within or near a promoter that interacts with regulatory proteins (repressors or activators) to control the transcription of an operon. While enhancers also assist transcription, they are typically located further away from the promoter, whereas the operator is the specific sequence \"by the promoter\" that functions as the regulatory switch.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
