    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most significant biological barrier to successful organ transplantation is the recipient's immune system identifying the donor organ as foreign tissue. This leads to an immunological response where the body attacks the transplant, a process known as graft rejection. Therefore, while logistics and matching are important, the primary biological reason for failure is the immune reaction.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
