    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Are the daughter nuclei formed during cleavage exactly equivalent , or is there some sort of parceling out of potentialities during cleavage?\n\nOptions: \nA. Partial segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nB. Partial segregation of genetic potentialities, influenced by environmental factors during cleavage\nC. Random parceling out of genetic potentialities independent of cleavage\nD. Segregation of genetic potentialities occurs, but only in specific cell lineages\nE. Segregation of genetic potentialities only in later stages\nF. Segregation of genetic potentialities with bias toward cellular location\nG. No segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nH. Segregation of genetic potentialities based on maternal and paternal origin\nI. Segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nJ. Equal segregation of genetic potentialities, but differential activation during cleavage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
