    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3199",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about the beak size of finches on the island of Daphne Major during prolonged drought is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. Each bird's beak size increased due to the abundance of food during the drought.\nB. Each bird developed a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nC. Each bird's beak became weaker and narrower as the drought persisted.\nD. Each bird evolved a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nE. Each bird's survival was not influenced by the depth and strength of its beak during the drought.\nF. Each bird that survived the drought produced only offspring with deeper, stronger beaks than seen in the previous generation.\nG. Each bird's beak size did not change during the drought.\nH. Each bird's survival was strongly influenced by the depth and strength of its beak as the drought persisted.\nI. Each bird's survival was only influenced by its ability to find water during the drought, not the size of its beak.\nJ. Each bird that survived the drought produced offspring with the same beak size as seen in the previous generation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "During the prolonged drought on Daphne Major, individual finches could not change their own beak morphology; instead, those with deeper, stronger beaks were better able to crack the remaining large, hard seeds and survived at higher rates. This is a classic example of natural selection where a physical trait directly influences survival probability during environmental stress. Therefore, while the average beak size of the *population* increased in the next generation, individual birds' beaks remained the same size throughout their lives.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
