    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the probability of getting exactly three heads infive flips of a balanced coin?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12.5 percent\nB. 40 percent\nC. 18.75 percent\nD. 25 percent\nE. 37.5 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 31.25 percent\nH. 50 percent\nI. 62.5 percent\nJ. 20 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of getting exactly three heads in five flips of a balanced coin, we use the binomial probability formula: $P(X=k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$. Here, $n=5$, $k=3$, and $p=0.5$, which gives $\\binom{5}{3} (0.5)^3 (0.5)^2 = 10 \\times 0.03125 = 0.3125$. Converting this to a percentage results in 31.25%.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
