    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $P(5 < X < 11)$ for a normal distribution with $\\mu = 9$ and $\\sigma = 3$, we first convert the values to standard $Z$-scores using the formula $Z = \\frac{X - \\mu}{\\sigma}$:\n1. For $X = 5$: $Z_1 = \\frac{5 - 9}{3} = -1.333$\n2. For $X = 11$: $Z_2 = \\frac{11 - 9}{3} = 0.667$\n\nUsing the standard normal table, $P(Z < 0.667) \\approx 0.7475$ and $P(Z < -1.333) \\approx 0.0912$. Calculating the difference $0.7475 - 0.0912$ yields approximately $0.6563$, which most closely aligns with option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
