    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The antisense (noncoding) strand of DNA is 5' ATG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 3' What is the a)sensestrand? b)mRNAtranscribed? c)polypeptidechain that is translated?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3' TAG GAT AAA GCT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' AUC CUA UUU CGA AAU UUG UCU CUC CUU AGA 3', Ile-Leu-Phe-Arg-Asn-Leu-Ser-Leu-Leu-Arg\nB. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu\nC. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTT AGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu\nD. 3' ATG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' UAC CUA UUU GUA AAU UUG UCU CUC CUU AGA 3', Tyr-Leu-Phe-Val-Asn-Leu-Ser-Leu-Leu-Arg\nE. 3' UAC CUA UUU CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTT AGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUC UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nF. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu\nG. 3' TAG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nH. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nI. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we follow the principles of DNA base pairing and transcription:\n1.  **Sense Strand (a):** This is the complement of the antisense strand (5' ATG GAT AAA GTT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 3'), written in the 3' to 5' direction. The complement is 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTT AGA 5'.\n2.  **mRNA (b):** Transcription occurs from the antisense strand; the mRNA sequence is identical to the sense strand but in the 5' to 3' direction with Uracil (U) instead of Thymine (T). Thus: 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3'.\n3.  **Polypeptide (c):** Using the genetic code: AUG(Met), GAU(Asp), AAA(Lys), GUU(Val), UUA(Leu), AAC(Asn), AGA(Arg), GAG(Glu), GAA(Glu), UCU(Ser).\n\n\\boxed{H}",
