    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compare cardiac muscle to skeletal and smooth muscle.\n\nOptions: \nA. Cardiac muscle has a metabolism similar to smooth muscle, designed for quick, short bursts of activity.\nB. Cardiac muscle cells are multinucleated and arranged in a non-striated pattern.\nC. Cardiac muscle shows some characteristics of both skeletal and smooth muscle. It is striated, has numerous nuclei per cell, is innervated by the autonomic nervous system, has intercalated discs, and its metabolism is designed for endurance.\nD. Cardiac muscle lacks intercalated discs, which differentiates it from skeletal and smooth muscle.\nE. Cardiac muscle does not have any similarities with skeletal and smooth muscle\nF. Cardiac muscle is innervated by the somatic nervous system, similar to skeletal muscle.\nG. Cardiac muscle is similar to skeletal muscle but not smooth muscle\nH. Cardiac muscle has a metabolism designed for speed and strength\nI. Cardiac muscle is not striated and has a single nucleus per cell, similar to smooth muscle.\nJ. Cardiac muscle is identical to smooth muscle in both structure and function.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
