    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2658",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Can an extra Y chromosome (XXY) modify behavior?\n\nOptions: \nA. The extra Y chromosome decreases a male's aggression\nB. The extra Y chromosome is linked to an increase in artistic skills\nC. The extra Y chromosome is associated with a significant decrease in risk-taking behavior\nD. The extra Y chromosome leads to a decrease in physical strength\nE. The extra Y chromosome is responsible for a man's level of intelligence\nF. The extra Y chromosome results in a higher level of empathy in males\nG. The extra Y chromosome causes a substantial increase in memory capacity\nH. The extra Y chromosome may predispose a male to a more aggressive attitude\nI. The extra Y chromosome has no effect on a male's behavior\nJ. The extra Y chromosome enhances a male's cognitive abilities significantly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Historically, the presence of an extra Y chromosome (XYY syndrome, though the prompt mistakenly notes XXY) was associated in controversial early studies with a predisposition toward increased aggression and impulsivity. While modern research suggests that most individuals with an extra Y chromosome lead normal lives, option H reflects the traditional hypothesis often discussed in behavioral genetics. (Note: XXY is Klinefelter syndrome, whereas XYY is the condition typically associated with the \"aggression\" debate).\n\n\\boxed{H}",
