    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3179",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How might you argue that the transmission of impulses does occur in plants?\n\nOptions: \nA. Impulse transmission in plants can be seen in the photosynthesis process\nB. Plants exhibit impulse transmission during pollination, when they attract pollinators to their flowers.\nC. The release of chemical signals in response to herbivore damage, triggering defense mechanisms, is an example of impulse transmission in plants.\nD. The reaction of the sensitive plant, Mimosapudica, to touch demonstrates that transmission of impulses does indeed occur in plants.\nE. The opening and closing of stomata in response to environmental stimuli indicate impulse transmission in plants.\nF. The movement of chloroplasts within plant cells in response to light demonstrates impulse transmission.\nG. The transmission of impulses in plants can be observed through the growth of roots\nH. The process of fruit ripening, which involves a complex interplay of hormones, is a form of impulse transmission in plants.\nI. The bending of plant stems toward a light source, known as phototropism, is evidence of impulse transmission.\nJ. The seed germination process proves the transmission of impulses in plants\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most direct and classic evidence for the transmission of impulses (specifically electrical action potentials similar to those in animals) is the rapid leaf-folding response of *Mimosa pudica*. When touched, an electrical signal travels from the point of stimulation to the pulvini (motor organs), causing a rapid loss of turgor pressure and subsequent movement. While other options describe important plant signaling, the sensitive plant's immediate reaction is the standard biological example of rapid impulse transmission.\n\nThe correct choice is \\boxed{D}.",
