      "generated_answer": "To find the expected value $\\langle w\\rangle$ of the number of heads when two fair coins are tossed, we list the possible outcomes for $w$: 0 (TT), 1 (HT, TH), and 2 (HH), with respective probabilities of 1/4, 2/4, and 1/4. The expected value is calculated as $\\langle w\\rangle = (0 \\times 1/4) + (1 \\times 2/4) + (2 \\times 1/4) = 0 + 0.5 + 0.5 = 1$. This corresponds to the mean number of successes in a binomial distribution with $n=2$ and $p=0.5$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
