    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4206",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are some 25,000ribosomesin an E. coli cell. If the structucalproteins of theseribosomeswere stretched out end to end as fully extended polypeptide chains, how many times could they encircle the E. coli cell?Assume that theribosomesare 180 \\AA in diameter, with a specific gravity of 1.0, and that they contain 40% protein. Assume that the E. coli cell is a sphere 1\\mu in diameter.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.10 × 10^4 times\nB. 1.26 × 10^4 times\nC. 0.80 × 10^4 times\nD. 3.50 × 10^4 times\nE. 1.76 × 10^4 times\nF. 3.00 × 10^4 times\nG. 4.00 × 10^4 times\nH. 2.54 × 10^4 times\nI. 1.00 × 10^4 times\nJ. 2.00 × 10^4 times\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the correct answer, we first calculate the total mass of the ribosomal proteins. \n\n1.  **Volume of one ribosome**: $V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (90 \\times 10^{-8} \\text{ cm})^3 \\approx 3.05 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ cm}^3$.\n2.  **Mass of protein per cell**: With a specific gravity of 1.0 and 40% protein content, one ribosome has $1.22 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ g}$ of protein. For 25,000 ribosomes, the total protein mass is $\\approx 3.05 \\times 10^{-14} \\text{ g}$.\n3.  **Total length**: Using the average molecular weight of an amino acid ($\\approx 110$ Da) and the length of an extended residue ($\\approx 3.6$ Å), the total length $L \\approx \\frac{3.05 \\times 10^{-14} \\text{ g} \\times 6.022 \\times 10^{23}}{110} \\times 3.6 \\text{ Å} \\approx 6.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ Å} = 0.06 \\text{ meters}$.\n4.  **Circumference**: The circumference of the cell is $\\pi \\times 1 \\mu\\text{m} \\approx 3.14 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{ m}$. Dividing the total length by the circumference yields approximately $1.9 \\times 10^4$ to $2.1 \\times 10^4$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
