    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3953",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number average and weight average molecular-weights are defined as M_n= [(\\sumN_i M_i) / (\\sumN_i)] = [1 / {{\\sum(w_i/ M_i)}}] and M_w = [(\\sumW_iM_i) / (\\sumW_i)] = [(\\sumN_i M^2_i) / (\\sumN_i M_i)] = \\sumw_iM_i respectively, where M_i = molecular weight of theithspecies N_i = moles of molecules with molecular weight M_i W_i= weight of material with molecular weight M_i w_i= weight fraction of molecules of theithspecies. Derive equations analogous to the ones above for the number average,X_n, and weight average,X_w, degree of polymerization.\n\nOptions: \nA. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)]\nB. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumW_i X_i)]\nC. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^0.5)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^1.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nD. X_n= [(\\sumw_i X_i) / (\\sumw_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^0.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nE. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)]\nF. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i^2 X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i^2)]\nG. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^3)]\nH. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nI. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nJ. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i X_i^2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The degree of polymerization $X_i$ is directly proportional to the molecular weight $M_i$ ($M_i = X_i M_0$, where $M_0$ is the formula weight of the repeating unit). By substituting $M_i = X_i M_0$ into the standard definitions for number average molecular weight ($M_n = \\sum N_i M_i / \\sum N_i$) and weight average molecular weight ($M_w = \\sum N_i M_i^2 / \\sum N_i M_i$), the constants $M_0$ cancel out or factor out to yield the corresponding averages for the degree of polymerization. Thus, $X_n = \\sum N_i X_i / \\sum N_i$ and $X_w = \\sum N_i X_i^2 / \\sum N_i X_i$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
