  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4187",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have two 1-liter containers connected to each other by a valve which is closed. In one container, you have liquid water in equilibrium with water vapor at 25°C. The other container contains a vacuum. Suddenly, you open the valve. Discuss the changes that take place, assuming temperature is constant with regard to (a) the vapor pressure, (b) the concentration of the water molecules in the vapor, (c) the number of molecules in the vapor state.\n\nOptions: \nA. Vapor pressure is halved, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is doubled, and the number of molecules is doubled\nB. Vapor pressure is unchanged, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is halved, and the number of molecules is doubled\nC. Vapor pressure, the concentration of the gaseous molecules and the number of molecules are all unchanged\nD. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is doubled, and the number of molecules is halved\nE. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is halved, and the number of molecules is unchanged\nF. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules are halved, the number of molecules remains unchanged\nG. Vapor pressure is halved, the concentration of the gaseous molecules remains unchanged, and the number of molecules is doubled\nH. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules remain unchanged, the number of molecules is doubled\nI. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules are doubled, the number of molecules remains unchanged\nJ. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules and the number of molecules remain unchanged\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, consider the principles of phase equilibrium:\n\n1.  **Vapor Pressure:** At a constant temperature, the vapor pressure of a pure substance depends only on the temperature. Once the valve is opened and equilibrium is re-established, the vapor pressure will return to its original value.\n2.  **Concentration:** Since $PV = nRT$ can be rewritten as $P = (n/V)RT$, and $P$ and $T$ are constant, the concentration ($n/V$) of the water molecules in the vapor phase remains unchanged.\n3.  **Number of Molecules:** The volume has doubled (from 1 liter to 2 liters); to maintain the same concentration and vapor pressure, the number of water molecules in the gas phase must double by evaporating more liquid water.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
