    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose C is a compact convex set in a linear normed space, and let T: C → C be a continuous mapping. Then, there exists a fixed point of T in C. Is this correct? Answer 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0\nB. 2.5\nC. -0.5\nD. 1.5\nE. -1.0\nF. 0.5\nG. 0.0\nH. 2.0\nI. -2.0\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
