    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6846",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company is interested in comparing the mean sales revenue per salesperson at two different locations. The manager takes a random sample of 10 salespeople from each location independently and records the sales revenue generated by each person during the last four weeks. He decides to use a t-test to compare the mean sales revenue at the two locations. Which of the following assumptions is necessary for the validity of the t-test?\n\nOptions: \nA. The population of the sales records at each location is not normally distributed.\nB. The population of the sales records at each location is normally distributed.\nC. The sample size at both locations is less than 30\nD. The population standard deviations at both locations are equal.\nE. The sales revenue is measured on an interval or ratio scale.\nF. The population of the sales records at each location follows a uniform distribution.\nG. The population standard deviations at both locations are not equal.\nH. The population standard deviations at both locations are known.\nI. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are not equal.\nJ. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are equal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
