      "generated_answer": "For a t-test to be valid, especially when dealing with small sample sizes (n = 10, which is less than 30), the underlying populations from which the samples are drawn must be approximately normally distributed. While other assumptions like interval/ratio scaling and independence are important, Option B is a fundamental parametric requirement for the t-distribution to accurately model the test statistic. Therefore, the necessity of a normal distribution is the most standard answer among the choices provided.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
