    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ms. Ling has been living in her home for exactly 4 years. She knows that there are 12 months in each year. She found the total number of months, m, she has been living in her home by using the number sentence below. 4 × 12 = m Which number sentence shows another way to find the total number of months, m, Ms. Ling has been living in her home?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12 ÷ m = 4\nB. m ÷ 4 = 12\nC. m × 4 = 12\nD. 12 × m = 4\nE. m - 12 = 4\nF. 4 × m = 12\nG. 4 + m = 12\nH. 12 – m = 4\nI. m - 4 = 12\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
