    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Using the triple product rule for partial derivatives (also known as the cyclic chain rule) for a function $F(x, y, z) = 0$, we have the identities:\n$\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial y} = -\\frac{F_y}{F_x}$, $\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial z} = -\\frac{F_z}{F_y}$, and $\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x} = -\\frac{F_x}{F_z}$.\nMultiplying these together yields:\n$\\left(-\\frac{F_y}{F_x}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{F_z}{F_y}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{F_x}{F_z}\\right) = -1$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
