    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $H'(1)$, we first differentiate $H(z) = \\int_0^1 e^{-z^2 t^2} dt$ with respect to $z$ using Leibniz's Rule:\n$H'(z) = \\int_0^1 \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} (e^{-z^2 t^2}) dt = \\int_0^1 -2zt^2 e^{-z^2 t^2} dt$.\nSetting $z=1$, we get $H'(1) = \\int_0^1 -2t^2 e^{-t^2} dt$. Using integration by parts ($u = t$, $dv = -2t e^{-t^2} dt$), we find $H'(1) = [t e^{-t^2}]_0^1 - \\int_0^1 e^{-t^2} dt = e^{-1} - \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}}{2} \\text{erf}(1) \\approx 0.36788 - 0.74682 = -0.37894$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
