    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7148",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate $\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 1^{{-}} \\prod_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}}(\\frac{{1+x^{{n+1}}{{1+x^n}})^{{x^n}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.3456789\nB. 2.7182818\nC. $\\infty$\nD. 4.5678901\nE. 0.73575888\nF. 0\nG. 1\nH. 1.23456789\nI. 3.456789\nJ. 1.1111111\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit $L = \\lim_{x \\to 1^-} \\prod_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\left( \\frac{1+x^{n+1}}{1+x^n} \\right)^{x^n}$, we take the natural logarithm:\n$\\ln L = \\lim_{x \\to 1^-} \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} x^n \\ln\\left( \\frac{1+x^{n+1}}{1+x^n} \\right)$.\nAs $x \\to 1^-$, the sum can be approximated by the integral $\\int_0^{\\infty} e^{-t} \\ln\\left( \\frac{1+e^{-t}}{1+e^{-t}} \\right) dt$ (using $x^n \\approx e^{-tn}$ where $t = 1-x$), but more directly, the expression is a known form related to the constant $e^{-1}$ or $e^1$. Numerical evaluation or specific series identities for this product show that as $x \\to 1^-$, the product approaches $e^{-1} \\approx 0.3678$ or $e^1 \\approx 2.71828$ depending on the exact structure; here, the terms simplify such that the limit evaluates to $1/e$ or $e$. However, the option B corresponds to the mathematical constant $e \\approx 2.7182818$, which is a common result for such limit structures.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
