    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7577",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $I(R)=\\iint_{{x^2+y^2 \\leq R^2}}(\\frac{{1+2 x^2}}{{1+x^4+6x^2y^2+y^4}}-\\frac{{1+y^2}}{{2+x^4+y^4}}) dx dy$. What is the limit of $I(R)$ as $R$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.123456\nB. 2.453232\nC. 0.999999\nD. 4.669201\nE. 2.718281\nF. 3.141593\nG. 1.53978589\nH. 3.567839\nI. 0\nJ. -1.234567\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
