  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7472",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sum the series $\\sum_{{m=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}}\\frac{{m^2 n}}{{3^m(n3^m+m3^n)}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.23456\nB. 0.41567\nC. 0.19375\nD. 0.28125\nE. 0.62500\nF. 0.14659\nG. 0.51234\nH. 0.33333\nI. 0.73145\nJ. 0.77777\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the given sum be $S$. We have:\n$S = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{m^2 n}{3^m(n 3^m + m 3^n)}$\n\nBy symmetry, swapping $m$ and $n$ gives the same total sum:\n$S = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{n^2 m}{3^n(m 3^n + n 3^m)}$\n\nAdding these two expressions together:\n$2S = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\frac{m^2 n}{3^m(n 3^m + m 3^n)} + \\frac{n^2 m}{3^n(n 3^m + m 3^n)} \\right)$\n$2S = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{m^2 n 3^n + n^2 m 3^m}{3^m 3^n (n 3^m + m 3^n)} = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{mn(m 3^n + n 3^m)}{3^m 3^n (n 3^m + m 3^n)} = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{mn}{3^{m+n}}$\n\nThis separates into two independent sums:\n$2S = \\left( \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{m}{3^m} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{n}{3^n} \\right)$\nUsing the formula $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} kx^k = \\frac{x}{(1-x)^2}$ for $|x| < 1$, with $x = 1/3$:\n$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{k}{3^k} = \\frac{1/3}{(1 - 1/3)^2} = \\frac{1/3}{4/9} = \\frac{3}{4}$\n$2S = \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{9}{16} \\implies S = \\frac{9}{32} = 0.28125$\n\n\\boxed{D}",
