    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6945",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For any poitie integer $n$, let $\\langle n\\rangle$ denote the closest integer to $\\sqrt{{n}}$. Evaluate $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{2^{{\\langle n \\rangle}}+2^{{-\\langle n \\rangle}}{{2^n}}$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 7.0\nB. 2.0\nC. 4.5\nD. 1.0\nE. 5.0\nF. 6.0\nG. 4.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 3.0\nJ. 8.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the sum $S = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{2^{\\langle n \\rangle} + 2^{-\\langle n \\rangle}}{2^n}$, we first determine the range of $n$ for which $\\langle n \\rangle = k$.\nThe condition $\\langle n \\rangle = k$ (where $k$ is the closest integer to $\\sqrt{n}$) is satisfied when $k - \\frac{1}{2} < \\sqrt{n} < k + \\frac{1}{2}$, which squares to $k^2 - k + \\frac{1}{4} < n < k^2 + k + \\frac{1}{4}$, meaning $n$ ranges from $k^2 - k + 1$ to $k^2 + k$ (a total of $2k$ terms for each $k$).\n\nThe sum can be rewritten by grouping terms with the same $k$:\n$S = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=k^2-k+1}^{k^2+k} \\frac{2^k + 2^{-k}}{2^n} = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} (2^k + 2^{-k}) \\sum_{n=k^2-k+1}^{k^2+k} \\frac{1}{2^n}$.\nThe inner sum is a geometric series: $\\sum_{n=k^2-k+1}^{k^2+k} \\frac{1}{2^n} = \\frac{1}{2^{k^2-k}} - \\frac{1}{2^{k^2+k}} = \\frac{2^{2k}-1}{2^{k^2+k}}$.\nSubstituting this back:\n$S = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(2^k + 2^{-k})(2^{2k}-1)}{2^{k^2+k}} = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{2^{3k} - 2^k + 2^k - 2^{-k}}{2^{k^2+k}} = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\frac{1}{2^{k^2-2k}} - \\frac{1}{2^{k^2+2k}} \\right)$.\nThis is a telescoping series where $a_k = \\frac{1}{2^{k^2-2k}}$. The sum is $(a_1 + a_2) = (\\frac{1}{2^{-1}} + \\frac{1}{2^0}) = 2 + 1 = 3$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
