    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find all c in Z_3 such that Z_3[x]/(x^3 + cx^2 + 1) is a field.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. -1\nC. 0\nD. 1\nE. -3\nF. 6\nG. 5\nH. -2\nI. 2\nJ. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine when the quotient ring $Z_3[x]/(x^3 + cx^2 + 1)$ is a field, the polynomial $f(x) = x^3 + cx^2 + 1$ must be irreducible over $Z_3$. Since $f(x)$ is a cubic, it is irreducible if and only if it has no roots in $Z_3 = \\{0, 1, 2\\}$.\n- If $x=0$, $f(0) = 1 \\neq 0$.\n- If $x=1$, $f(1) = 1^3 + c(1^2) + 1 = 2 + c \\equiv 0 \\pmod 3 \\implies c = 1$. (Thus $c \\neq 1$)\n- If $x=2$, $f(2) = 2^3 + c(2^2) + 1 = 8 + 4c + 1 = 9 + 4c \\equiv c \\pmod 3$.\nFor $f(x)$ to have no roots, we must have $c \\not\\equiv 1 \\pmod 3$ and $c \\not\\equiv 0 \\pmod 3$, which leaves $c \\equiv 2 \\pmod 3$ as the only possibility.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
