    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7146",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The function f: U_5 \to U_5 given by f(x) = x^2 is a homomorphism. What is K_f?\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, 2]\nB. [2, 5]\nC. [4, 2]\nD. [5, 2]\nE. [3, 5]\nF. [0, 1]\nG. [3, 4]\nH. [4, 1]\nI. [1, 5]\nJ. [2, 3]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this, we first identify the elements of the group $U_5$. $U_5$ (the multiplicative group of integers modulo 5) consists of the elements $\\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$. The kernel $K_f$ of a homomorphism is the set of elements in the domain that map to the identity element of the codomain (which is 1 in $U_5$).\n\nCalculating $f(x) = x^2 \\pmod{5}$ for each element:\n- $f(1) = 1^2 = 1 \\pmod{5}$\n- $f(2) = 2^2 = 4 \\pmod{5}$\n- $f(3) = 3^2 = 9 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}$\n- $f(4) = 4^2 = 16 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$\n\nThe elements that map to 1 are $\\{1, 4\\}$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
