  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7101",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the xy-plane, the graph of x^(log y) = y^log x is\n\nOptions: \nA. a closed loop in the open first quadrant\nB. two separate points\nC. a single point\nD. the entire xy-plane\nE. a ray in the open first quadrant\nF. an open second quadrant\nG. the open first quadrant\nH. a closed curve\nI. a line through the origin\nJ. a parabolic curve in the open first quadrant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the equation $x^{\\log y} = y^{\\log x}$, we first note that the logarithmic functions $\\log x$ and $\\log y$ are defined only for $x > 0$ and $y > 0$, meaning the graph must be in the open first quadrant. Taking the logarithm of both sides gives $\\log(x^{\\log y}) = \\log(y^{\\log x})$, which simplifies to $(\\log y)(\\log x) = (\\log x)(\\log y)$. This equation is an identity that holds true for all $x, y \\in (0, \\infty)$, meaning every point in the open first quadrant satisfies the equation.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{G}.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 163,
