    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7343",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose f is an analytic function defined on $\\{{z \\in C : IM(z) > 0\\}}$, the upper half plane. Given the information that f(f(z)) = z and f'(z) = 1/z^2 for every z. Find the most general possible expression of f(z). What is f(2)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1\nB. -1\nC. 2\nD. 0.5\nE. -i\nF. i\nG. 4\nH. -4\nI. -0.5\nJ. -2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $f(2)$, we analyze the given conditions:\n1. $f'(z) = \\frac{1}{z^2}$ implies that $f(z) = -\\frac{1}{z} + C$ for some constant $C$.\n2. The condition $f(f(z)) = z$ (involution) must hold:\n   $f(f(z)) = -\\frac{1}{-\\frac{1}{z} + C} + C = -\\frac{1}{\\frac{-1 + Cz}{z}} + C = \\frac{-z}{-1 + Cz} + C = \\frac{-z + C(-1 + Cz)}{-1 + Cz} = \\frac{C^2z - z - C}{Cz - 1}$.\n3. For this to equal $z$, the numerator $C^2z - z - C$ must equal $z(Cz - 1) = Cz^2 - z$. Comparing coefficients, we see $C$ must be $0$.\nThus, $f(z) = -1/z$. Plugging in $z = 2$ gives $f(2) = -1/2 = -0.5$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
