  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6947",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose sequence x_n satisfies x_n*x_{{n+1}}=n for all n>=1, and $\\lim_{{n\\rightarrow\\infty}}\\frac{{x_n}}{{x_{{n+1}}=1$. What's the value of $\\pi*x_1^2$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.14\nB. 2.0\nC. 4.0\nD. 2.5\nE. 6.0\nF. 5.0\nG. 0.5\nH. 1.0\nI. 3.5\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Given the recurrence relation $x_n x_{n+1} = n$, we have:\n1. $x_1 x_2 = 1$\n2. $x_2 x_3 = 2$\n3. $x_3 x_4 = 3$, and so on.\n\nBy substituting terms, we find $x_2 = \\frac{1}{x_1}$, $x_3 = \\frac{2}{x_2} = 2x_1$, $x_4 = \\frac{3}{x_3} = \\frac{3}{2x_1}$, and $x_5 = \\frac{4}{x_4} = \\frac{4 \\cdot 2}{3} x_1$.\nIn general, for even terms $x_{2n} = \\frac{(2n-1)!!}{(2n-2)!!} \\frac{1}{x_1}$ and for odd terms $x_{2n+1} = \\frac{(2n)!!}{(2n-1)!!} x_1$.\n\nThe condition $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{x_n}{x_{n+1}} = 1$ implies $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{x_{2n+1}}{x_{2n}} = 1$.\nSubstituting the general forms:\n$\\frac{x_{2n+1}}{x_{2n}} = \\frac{(2n)!! x_1}{(2n-1)!!} \\cdot \\frac{(2n-2)!! x_1}{(2n-1)!!} = x_1^2 \\cdot \\frac{[(2n)!!]^2}{[(2n-1)!!]^2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n}$.\nWallis' product formula states that $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{[(2n)!!]^2}{[(2n-1)!!]^2 (2n+1)} = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\nAs $n \\to \\infty$, $\\frac{2n+1}{2n} \\to 1$, so $x_1^2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 1$, which gives $x_1^2 = \\frac{2}{\\pi}$.\nThus, $\\pi x_1^2 = \\pi (\\frac{2}{\\pi}) = 2.0$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
