    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the domain of $h(x) = \\sqrt{25-x^2} + \\sqrt{-(x-2)}$, we must satisfy the conditions for both square roots:\n1.  $25 - x^2 \\geq 0 \\implies x^2 \\leq 25 \\implies -5 \\leq x \\leq 5$.\n2.  $-(x-2) \\geq 0 \\implies x-2 \\leq 0 \\implies x \\leq 2$.\n\nTaking the intersection of these two intervals, we get $-5 \\leq x \\leq 2$, which is the interval $[-5, 2]$. The width of this interval is $2 - (-5) = 7$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
