    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7446",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the graph of a certain function $f(x)$ is shifted $2$ units to the right and stretched vertically by a factor of $2$ (meaning that all $y$-coordinates are doubled), the resulting figure is identical to the original graph. Given that $f(0)=0.1$, what is $f(10)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01\nB. 32\nC. 3.2\nD. 5\nE. 1\nF. 0.2\nG. 0.5\nH. 2\nI. 10\nJ. 20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The transformations applied to the function $f(x)$ are a horizontal shift of 2 units to the right ($f(x-2)$) and a vertical stretch by a factor of 2 ($2f(x-2)$). Since the resulting figure is identical to the original graph, we have the functional equation $f(x) = 2f(x-2)$, or equivalently, $f(x+2) = \\frac{1}{2}f(x)$.\n\nGiven $f(0) = 0.1$, we can apply the relation repeatedly to find $f(10)$:\n$f(2) = \\frac{1}{2}f(0) = \\frac{0.1}{2} = 0.05$\n$f(4) = \\frac{1}{2}f(2) = 0.025$\n...\n$f(x+2k) = (\\frac{1}{2})^k f(x)$.\nFor $x=0$ and $k=5$, $f(10) = (\\frac{1}{2})^5 f(0) = \\frac{1}{32} \\times 0.1 = \\frac{0.1}{32} = 0.003125$.\n\nHowever, re-reading the problem: \"stretched vertically... the resulting figure is identical to the original graph\" means $2f(x-2) = f(x)$.\nThen $f(x) = 2f(x-2)$.\n$f(2) = 2f(0) = 0.2$\n$f(4) = 2f(2) = 0.4$\n$f(6) = 2f(4) = 0.8$\n$f(8) = 2f(6) = 1.6$\n$f(10) = 2f(8) = 3.2$\n\n\\boxed{C}",
