    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the greatest common divisor of $2^{{1001}}-1$ and $2^{{1012}}-1$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1024\nB. 2049\nC. 2048\nD. 4096\nE. 2\nF. 4095\nG. 1\nH. 511\nI. 2047\nJ. 2050\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers of the form $2^a - 1$ and $2^b - 1$, we use the property $\\gcd(2^a - 1, 2^b - 1) = 2^{\\gcd(a, b)} - 1$. \n\n1. First, find the GCD of the exponents: $\\gcd(1001, 1012)$. Using the Euclidean algorithm, $\\gcd(1012, 1001) = \\gcd(1001, 1012 - 1001) = \\gcd(1001, 11)$. Since $1001 = 11 \\times 91$, the GCD is 11.\n2. Substitute this back into the formula: $\\gcd(2^{1001} - 1, 2^{1012} - 1) = 2^{11} - 1$.\n3. Calculate the value: $2^{11} - 1 = 2048 - 1 = 2047$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
