    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The maximum number of acute angles in a convex 10-gon in the Euclidean plane is\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 2\nC. 7\nD. 9\nE. 4\nF. 6\nG. 1\nH. 5\nI. 8\nJ. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In a convex $n$-gon, the sum of the exterior angles is always $360^\\circ$. For an interior angle to be acute (less than $90^\\circ$), the corresponding exterior angle must be obtuse (greater than $90^\\circ$); since the sum of exterior angles is $360^\\circ$, there can be at most three such obtuse exterior angles ($4 \\times 90^\\circ = 360^\\circ$, so four or more would exceed the sum unless the polygon is non-convex). This rule applies to any convex polygon with $n \\geq 3$ sides, meaning the maximum number of acute angles is 3.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
