      "generated_answer": "The region defined by $|x| + |y| < 1$ is a square with vertices at $(1, 0)$, $(0, 1)$, $(-1, 0)$, and $(0, -1)$, which has a total area of $2$. The condition $2(x+y) > 1$ simplifies to $y > -x + \\frac{1}{2}$, representing the area above the line $y = -x + 0.5$ within the square. This specific sub-region is a triangle with vertices at $(0.5, 0)$, $(1, 0)$, and $(0, 1)$, which has an area of $\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 0.5 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{4}$. The probability is the ratio of this triangular area to the total area: $\\frac{1/4}{2} = \\frac{1}{8}$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
