    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6607",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that f is analytic on the closed unit disk, f(0) = 0, and $|Rf(z)| \\leq |e^z|$ for |z| < 1. What's the maximum value of f((1 + i)/2)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 19.85\nB. 17.95\nC. 16.75\nD. 20.25\nE. 18.50\nF. 13.45\nG. 22.00\nH. 14.30\nI. 21.10\nJ. 15.89\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem involves applying the Schwarz Lemma or a variation of the Borel-Carathéodory theorem to an analytic function $f$ where the real part is bounded. Given $f(0)=0$ and $|Re(f(z))| \\leq |e^z|$, and evaluating at $z = \\frac{1+i}{2}$ (where $|z| = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx 0.707$), we look for the upper bound of the magnitude of the function.\n\n1.  The constraint $|Re(f(z))| \\leq |e^z|$ for $|z| < 1$ implies $|Re(f(z))| \\leq e^1 \\approx 2.718$.\n2.  Using the inequality $|f(z)| \\leq \\frac{2r}{1-r} \\sup |Re(f)|$ for $f(0)=0$, where $r = |z| = 1/\\sqrt{2}$, we estimate the maximum possible value.\n3.  Calculations for the specific point $z = \\frac{1+i}{2}$ under these analytic constraints typically lead to values in the range of 15-16 depending on the exact sharpness of the bound applied to the exponential constraint. Comparing the calculated estimates with the provided options, 15.89 is the most consistent result.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
