      "generated_answer": "To find the sum of all integer solutions to $|n| < |n-3| < 9$, we solve the inequalities separately:\n1. $|n| < |n-3|$ implies $n < 1.5$ (by squaring both sides or checking the midpoint).\n2. $|n-3| < 9$ implies $-9 < n-3 < 9$, which simplifies to $-6 < n < 12$.\nCombining these, we have $-6 < n < 1.5$, giving the integer solutions $n \\in \\{-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1\\}$. The sum is $(-5) + (-4) + (-3) + (-2) + (-1) + 0 + 1 = -14$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
