    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6952",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the value of the inflection point of f(x) =(10 ln(x))/(x^2)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.000\nB. 1.587\nC. 0.693\nD. 1.203\nE. 3.014\nF. 2.718\nG. 4.000\nH. 3.142\nI. 1.000\nJ. 2.301\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inflection point, we need to find where the second derivative $f''(x)$ is zero or undefined.\n\n1.  **First derivative:** Using the quotient rule on $f(x) = 10 \\cdot \\frac{\\ln(x)}{x^2}$:\n    $f'(x) = 10 \\left( \\frac{x^2(\\frac{1}{x}) - \\ln(x)(2x)}{x^4} \\right) = 10 \\left( \\frac{x - 2x \\ln(x)}{x^4} \\right) = \\frac{10(1 - 2 \\ln(x))}{x^3}$.\n2.  **Second derivative:**\n    $f''(x) = 10 \\left( \\frac{x^3(-\\frac{2}{x}) - (1 - 2 \\ln(x))(3x^2)}{x^6} \\right) = \\frac{10x^2(-2 - 3 + 6 \\ln(x))}{x^6} = \\frac{10(6 \\ln(x) - 5)}{x^4}$.\n3.  **Solving $f''(x) = 0$:**\n    $6 \\ln(x) - 5 = 0 \\implies \\ln(x) = \\frac{5}{6} \\implies x = e^{5/6} \\approx 2.30097$.\n\nRounding to three decimal places gives $2.301$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
