      "generated_answer": "To find $g(25)$, we set the input of $g$, which is $f(x)$, equal to $25$:\n$f(x) = 3x^2 - 2 = 25 \\implies 3x^2 = 27 \\implies x^2 = 9 \\implies x = 3$ or $x = -3$.\nSince $g(f(x)) = x^2 + x + 1$, we evaluate this expression for both possible values of $x$:\nIf $x = 3$, $g(25) = 3^2 + 3 + 1 = 13$.\nIf $x = -3$, $g(25) = (-3)^2 + (-3) + 1 = 9 - 3 + 1 = 7$.\nThe sum of all possible values of $g(25)$ is $13 + 7 = 20$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
