      "generated_answer": "To find the smallest amount of work required, we assume a reversible (Carnot) heat pump. First, convert the temperatures to Kelvin: $T_L = 7 + 273 = 280\\text{ K}$ and $T_H = 27 + 273 = 300\\text{ K}$.\n\nThe Coefficient of Performance (COP) for heating is given by $COP = \\frac{T_H}{T_H - T_L} = \\frac{300}{300 - 280} = \\frac{300}{20} = 15$.\nThe work required is $W = \\frac{Q_H}{COP} = \\frac{15,000\\text{ J}}{15} = 1,000\\text{ J}$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
