    "global index": "MathQA_2532",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the smallest value of n , for which 2 n is not a prime number , is\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 3\nC. 4\nD. 1\nE. 3\nF. 5\nG. 2\nH. 5\nI. 6\nJ. 4\nK. 8\nL. 9\nM. 12\nN. 14\nO. 16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the smallest value of $n$ for which $2n$ is not a prime number, we evaluate the expression starting from the smallest possible natural number for $n$ (typically $n=1$). \n\n1. If $n=1$, then $2n = 2(1) = 2$. Since 2 is a prime number, we move to the next value.\n2. If $n=2$, then $2n = 2(2) = 4$. Since 4 is a composite number (not prime), $n=2$ is the smallest value for which $2n$ is not prime.\n\nComparing this result to the given options, the value 2 corresponds to letters A and G.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
