      "generated_answer": "To find the number of level-2 employees without college degrees, we can set up the following calculations:\n1. Let $T$ be the total number of sales staff. Since level-1 college graduates (20 people) account for 10% of the staff, $0.10T = 20$, meaning $T = 200$.\n2. Because college graduates and non-graduates are equally represented, there are 100 staff members without college degrees.\n3. Out of 72 level-1 employees, 20 are graduates, so $72 - 20 = 52$ are non-graduates; therefore, the number of level-2 non-graduates is $100 - 52 = 48$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
