      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of the rancher lassoing the cow at least once in 3 attempts, it is easiest to calculate the complement: the probability that he fails in all 3 attempts. \n\n1. Since the success rate is $1/3$, the probability of failure in a single throw is $1 - 1/3 = 2/3$.\n2. The probability of failing 3 times in a row is $(2/3) \\times (2/3) \\times (2/3) = 8/27$.\n3. The probability of succeeding at least once is $1 - 8/27 = 19/27$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
