    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the cost difference, we set up a system of linear equations where $s$ is the price of shoes and $b$ is the price of boots:\n1) $22s + 16b = 540$\n2) $8s + 32b = 720$\n\nDividing the first equation by 2 gives $11s + 8b = 270$ (so $8b = 270 - 11s$). Substituting $32b = 4(270 - 11s)$ into the second equation: $8s + 1080 - 44s = 720 \\Rightarrow 36s = 360$, so $s = 10$.\nPlugging $s = 10$ into $8s + 32b = 720$ gives $80 + 32b = 720 \\Rightarrow 32b = 640$, so $b = 20$. The difference is $20 - 10 = 10$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
