      "generated_answer": "To find the total salary pool after the headcount reduction compared to before, we use the formula: $\\text{Total Salary} = \\text{Average Salary} \\times \\text{Number of Employees}$.\n\n1. Let the original number of employees be $E$ and the original average salary be $A$; the original total pool is $E \\times A$.\n2. After the reduction, the number of employees is $0.94E$ (since 6% were fired) and the new average salary is $1.10A$ (a 10% increase).\n3. The new total pool is $(0.94E) \\times (1.10A) = 1.034 \\times (E \\times A)$, which represents 103.4% of the original pool.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
