      "generated_answer": "To find the rate of interest ($R$), we use the difference between Compound Interest (CI) and Simple Interest (SI) for 2 years. \n1. The SI for 1 year is $\\frac{324}{2} = 162$.\n2. The difference between CI and SI for 2 years ($340 - 324 = 16$) is the interest earned on the first year's interest.\n3. Therefore, $R = (\\frac{16}{162}) \\times 100 \\approx 9.876\\%$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
