    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: what is the range of all the roots of | x ^ 2 - 3 | = x ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 3\nC. 2\nD. 1\nE. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the range of the roots, we solve $|x^2 - 3| = x$ by considering two cases:\n1. $x^2 - 3 = x \\implies x^2 - x - 3 = 0$, giving $x = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2}$ (the negative root is discarded since $x$ must be $\\ge 0$).\n2. $-(x^2 - 3) = x \\implies x^2 + x - 3 = 0$, giving $x = \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2}$ (the negative root is discarded).\n\nThe roots are $x_1 = \\frac{\\sqrt{13} + 1}{2}$ and $x_2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{13} - 1}{2}$, and their range is the difference between the largest and smallest values: $\\frac{\\sqrt{13} + 1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{13} - 1}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
