    "global index": "MathQA_518",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if f ( f ( n ) ) + f ( n ) = 2 n + 3 and f ( 0 ) = 1 , what is the value of f ( 2012 ) ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 222\nB. 2787\nC. 2013\nD. 2778\nE. 10222\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $f(n)$, we assume a linear form $f(n) = an + b$. Substituting this into the equation $f(f(n)) + f(n) = 2n + 3$, we get $a(an+b) + b + an + b = 2n + 3$, which simplifies to $(a^2 + a)n + ab + 2b = 2n + 3$.\n\nSolving for $a$ and $b$:\n1. $a^2 + a = 2 \\implies (a+2)(a-1) = 0$. Since $f(0)=1$ and the output increases with $n$, we test $a=1$.\n2. If $a=1$, then $1(b) + 2b = 3 \\implies 3b = 3 \\implies b = 1$.\nThus, $f(n) = n + 1$, which satisfies $f(0)=1$ and $f(f(n)) + f(n) = (n+2) + (n+1) = 2n+3$.\n\nFor $n=2012$, $f(2012) = 2012 + 1 = 2013$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
