    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $L$ be the length of the longer piece. Since the total length of the wire is 12, the cut point $x$ (from one end) must be such that the longer piece $L$ is greater than 6 ($L > 6$).\nIf the longer piece forms a square with area $> 4$, then its side $s$ must be $> 2$, meaning the perimeter $L = 4s > 8$.\nGiven the wire is cut at an arbitrary point $x \\in [0, 12]$, the longer piece has length $L = \\max(x, 12-x)$; for $L > 8$, the cut must occur in the intervals $0 \\le x < 4$ or $8 < x \\le 12$, which have a combined length of $4 + 4 = 8$ out of the total 12. Thus, the probability is $8/12 = 2/3$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
