    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if a 5 cm cube is cut into 1 cm cubes , then what is the percentage increase in the surface area of the resulting cubes ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100 %\nB. 200 %\nC. 300 %\nD. 400 %\nE. 500 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the percentage increase, we first calculate the initial and final surface areas:\n1.  **Initial Surface Area:** A $5 \\text{ cm}$ cube has a surface area of $6 \\times (5^2) = 150 \\text{ cm}^2$.\n2.  **Final Surface Area:** Cutting it into $1 \\text{ cm}$ cubes yields $5^3 = 125$ small cubes, each with a surface area of $6 \\times (1^2) = 6 \\text{ cm}^2$, totaling $125 \\times 6 = 750 \\text{ cm}^2$.\n3.  **Percentage Increase:** The increase is $750 - 150 = 600$; the percentage increase is $(600 / 150) \\times 100 = 400\\%$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
