    "global index": "MathQA_1301",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a lady starts from p towards q and realizes that at a point r , if he walks 50 km further he will be at a point s , which is as far away from r as it is from q . what is the distance between p and q if the distance between p and r is half the distance from r to q ? ( assume that p , q , r and s are all on the same straight line )\n\nOptions: \nA. 150 km\nB. 200 km\nC. 250 km\nD. 125 km\nE. 155 km\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the distance between P and Q, we can represent the points on a straight line:\n1. Let the distance $PR = x$. According to the problem, $PR$ is half the distance of $RQ$, so $RQ = 2x$. The total distance $PQ = x + 2x = 3x$.\n2. Point $S$ is 50 km from $R$ ($RS = 50$). The problem states $S$ is as far from $R$ as it is from $Q$, meaning $S$ is the midpoint of $RQ$, so $RS = SQ = 50$.\n3. Since $RS = 50$ and $RQ = 2 \\times RS$, then $RQ = 100$. Given $PR = \\frac{1}{2}RQ$, then $PR = 50$. Thus, $PQ = 50 + 100 = 150$ km.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
