    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The sum of any two odd integers is odd.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**. An odd integer can be represented as $2n + 1$ and another as $2m + 1$; their sum is $(2n + 1) + (2m + 1) = 2n + 2m + 2$, which is $2(n + m + 1)$. Since the result is divisible by 2, the sum of any two odd integers is always even.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
