    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find a recursion equation satisfying y [n] where y [n] is the sum of the squares of all integers from 0 to n.\n\nOptions: \nA. y [n-1] = y [n] + n^2; n \\geq 1 where y [0] = 0\nB. y [n] = (n(n+1)(2n+1))/6; n \\geq 0\nC. y [n-1] = y [n] * n^2; n \\geq 1 where y [0] = 0\nD. y [n-1] = y [n] / n^2; n \\geq 1 where y [0] = 0\nE. y [n+1] = 2y [n] + (n+1)^2; n \\geq 0 where y [0] = 0\nF. y [n-1] = y [n] - n^2; n \\geq 1 where y [0] = 0\nG. y [n] = y [n-1] + 2n - 1; n \\geq 1 where y [0] = 0\nH. y [n+1] = y [n] - (n+1)^2; n \\geq 0 where y [0] = 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
