    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A card is drawn at random from a deck of cards. Find the probability that at least one of the following three events will occur: Event A : a heart is drawn. Event B: a card which is not a face card is drawn. Event C: the number of spots (if any) on the drawn card is divisible by 3.\n\nOptions: \nA. 40/52\nB. 31/52\nC. 33/52\nD. 44/52\nE. 45/52\nF. 43/52\nG. 30/52\nH. 38/52\nI. 41/52\nJ. 35/52\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of the union of events A, B, and C ($P(A \\cup B \\cup C)$), it is easiest to find the complement: the probability that none of the events occur. For a card to satisfy none of the criteria, it must not be a heart (39 cards remaining), it must be a face card (Jack, Queen, King), and its rank must not be divisible by 3 (though face cards typically have no numerical spots, the prompt specifies \"if any,\" and standard face cards are not valued at 3, 6, or 9). There are 3 face cards (J, Q, K) in each of the 3 non-heart suits (Spades, Diamonds, Clubs), totaling $3 \\times 3 = 9$ cards that fail all three conditions. Thus, the probability of at least one event occurring is $1 - \\frac{9}{52} = \\frac{43}{52}$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
