    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given that the joint density function of the random variables X, Y and Z is f(x, y, z) = e-(x+y+z)when 0 < x < \\infty, 0 < y < \\infty, 0 < z < \\infty, find the cumulative distribution function F(x, y, z) of X,Y, and Z.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 - e^-(x+y+z) for x, y, z > 0\nB. e^-(x*y*z) for x, y, z > 0\nC. (1 - e^-x) / (1 - e^-y) / (1 - e^-z) for x, y, z > 0\nD. (1 - e^-x) (1 - e^-y) / (1 - e^-z) for x, y, z > 0\nE. e^-(1/x + 1/y + 1/z) for x, y, z > 0\nF. (1 - e^-x) (1 - e^-y) (1 - e^-z) for x, y, z > 0\nG. (e^-x - 1) (e^-y - 1) (e^-z - 1) for x, y, z > 0\nH. (1 - e^-2x) (1 - e^-2y) (1 - e^-2z) for x, y, z > 0\nI. (1 - e^-x) + (1 - e^-y) + (1 - e^-z) for x, y, z > 0\nJ. e^-x * e^-y * e^-z for x, y, z > 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
