      "generated_answer": "The problem asks for the mathematical representation or a calculation related to the pattern of a uniform linear array. The total field strength $E_T$ is the sum of a geometric progression:\n$E_T = E_0 \\left| \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} e^{j k \\psi} \\right| = E_0 \\left| \\frac{1 - e^{jn\\psi}}{1 - e^{j\\psi}} \\right| = E_0 \\left| \\frac{\\sin(n\\psi/2)}{\\sin(\\psi/2)} \\right|$.\n\nThe question ends with \"Compute the pattern of such a linear array,\" but the options provided are specific decimal values. Given the context of standard textbook problems (like those by Kraus or Jordan & Balmain), such a value often refers to the magnitude of the first side lobe relative to the main lobe for a specific $n$ (e.g., as $n$ becomes large, the first side lobe level of a uniform array is approximately $2/(3\\pi) \\approx 0.212$).\n\nBased on the standard characteristics of uniform linear arrays where the first side lobe level is approximately $0.212$ of the maximum field strength, Option C is the most scientifically recognized value in this context.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
