  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10345",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The statistical data for a certain community indicate that 25% of all girls are blondes, 50% of all girls and 75% of all blondes have blue eyes. If it is known that a girl has blue eyes, how much additional information is available if one is told that she is also a blonde?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.85 bits\nB. 1 bit\nC. 2 bits\nD. 0.5 bits\nE. 1.25 bits\nF. 0.75 bits\nG. 0.25 bits\nH. 1.75 bits\nI. 1.415 bits\nJ. 1.6 bits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the additional information, we use the formula $I = \\log_2(1/P(A|B))$, where $P(A|B)$ is the probability that the girl is blonde given she has blue eyes. \n\n1. Given: $P(\\text{Blonde}) = 0.25$, $P(\\text{Blue Eyes}) = 0.50$, and $P(\\text{Blue Eyes} | \\text{Blonde}) = 0.75$.\n2. Using Bayes' Theorem, $P(\\text{Blonde} | \\text{Blue Eyes}) = \\frac{P(\\text{Blue Eyes} | \\text{Blonde}) \\cdot P(\\text{Blonde})}{P(\\text{Blue Eyes})} = \\frac{0.75 \\cdot 0.25}{0.50} = 0.375$.\n3. The additional information is $I = -\\log_2(0.375) = -\\log_2(3/8) = \\log_2(8) - \\log_2(3) \\approx 3 - 1.585 = 1.415$ bits.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
