    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse z-transform of $F(z) = \\frac{2z^2 - 2z}{(z - 3)(z - 5)^2}$, we perform partial fraction expansion on $\\frac{F(z)}{z} = \\frac{2z - 2}{(z - 3)(z - 5)^2}$:\n$\\frac{2z - 2}{(z - 3)(z - 5)^2} = \\frac{A}{z - 3} + \\frac{B}{z - 5} + \\frac{C}{(z - 5)^2}$\nSolving for the constants gives $A = \\frac{2(3)-2}{(3-5)^2} = \\frac{4}{4} = 1$, $C = \\frac{2(5)-2}{5-3} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4$, and $B = -1$.\nSubstituting back, $F(z) = \\frac{z}{z - 3} - \\frac{z}{z - 5} + \\frac{4z}{(z - 5)^2}$, which transforms to $f[n] = 3^n u[n] - 5^n u[n] + \\frac{4}{5}n 5^n u[n] = 3^n u[n] + (\\frac{4}{5}n - 1) 5^n u[n]$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, and accounting for a potential typo in the question's representation of the first term ($3^n$ vs $3n$), Option D is the closest structural match.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
