  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10334",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A three input information channel with all three input symbols equally probable, is defined by the channel matrix, \\vert0.50.30.2\\vert \\vert0.20.30.5\\vert \\vert0.30.30.4\\vert Assuming that a maximum-likelihood decision rule is used, determine the error probability, P_E, of the channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. (13) / (30)\nB. (19) / (30)\nC. (15) / (30)\nD. (18) / (30)\nE. (14) / (30)\nF. (17) / (30)\nG. (21) / (30)\nH. (12) / (30)\nI. (16) / (30)\nJ. (20) / (30)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the error probability $P_E$ using a maximum-likelihood (ML) decision rule, we examine the channel matrix where rows represent inputs ($X$) and columns represent outputs ($Y$). The ML rule assigns an output $y_j$ to the input $x_i$ that maximizes $P(y_j|x_i)$ (the column maximum).\n\n1.  **Analyze the matrix $P(Y|X)$:**\n    Row 1 ($x_1$): [0.5, 0.3, 0.2]\n    Row 2 ($x_2$): [0.2, 0.3, 0.5]\n    Row 3 ($x_3$): [0.3, 0.3, 0.4]\n\n2.  **Determine Correct Detections ($P_C$):**\n    The ML rule selects the maximum value in each column to calculate the probability of correct transmission for each input $x_i$, weighted by $P(x_i) = 1/3$:\n    $P_C = \\sum P(x_i) \\cdot P(\\text{correct}|x_i) = \\frac{1}{3} (0.5 \\text{ from } x_1 + 0.3 \\text{ from } x_2 \\text{ or } x_1/x_3 + 0.5 \\text{ from } x_2) = \\frac{0.5 + 0.3 + 0.5}{3} = \\frac{1.3}{3} = \\frac{13}{30}$.\n\n3.  **Calculate Error Probability ($P_E$):**\n    $P_E = 1 - P_C = 1 - \\frac{13}{30} = \\frac{17}{30}$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
