    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Fourier sine series of $f(x) = x^2$ on $(0, 1)$, we calculate the coefficients $b_n = 2 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\sin(n\\pi x) dx$. Using integration by parts twice, we get $b_n = 2 \\left[ \\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi} + \\frac{2((-1)^n - 1)}{n^3\\pi^3} \\right]$, which can be rearranged to match the signs in option I. Factoring out the constants leads to the expression $b_n = 2 \\left[ \\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi} - \\frac{2[1 - (-1)^n]}{n^3\\pi^3} \\right]$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
