    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s) = \\frac{2s^2 - 4}{(s - 2)(s + 1)(s - 3)}$, we use partial fraction decomposition:\n$F(s) = \\frac{A}{s - 2} + \\frac{B}{s + 1} + \\frac{C}{s - 3}$\n1. For $A$ (at $s=2$): $A = \\frac{2(2)^2 - 4}{(2+1)(2-3)} = \\frac{4}{(3)(-1)} = -\\frac{4}{3}$.\n2. For $B$ (at $s=-1$): $B = \\frac{2(-1)^2 - 4}{(-1-2)(-1-3)} = \\frac{-2}{(-3)(-4)} = -\\frac{2}{12} = -\\frac{1}{6}$.\n3. For $C$ (at $s=3$): $C = \\frac{2(3)^2 - 4}{(3-2)(3+1)} = \\frac{14}{(1)(4)} = \\frac{7}{2}$.\nThe inverse Laplace transform is $f(t) = -\\frac{4}{3}e^{2t} - \\frac{1}{6}e^{-t} + \\frac{7}{2}e^{3t}$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
