    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transforms (a) L^-1{{2s / (s^2 + 1)^2}}, (b) L^-1{{1 / \\surds}}\n\nOptions: \nA. t sin t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \bullet (1 / \\surdt)\nB. cos t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \\cdot t e^{{-t^2}}\nC. e^t sin t, (1 / 2\\surd\\pi) \\cdot t\nD. t cos t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \bullet (1 / \\surdt)\nE. t^2 sin t, (1 / 2\\surd\\pi) \\cdot (1 / \\surdt)\nF. t tan t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \bullet (1 / \\surdt)\nG. t^2 e^t, (1 / 2\\surd\\pi) \\cdot e^{{-t^2}}\nH. t sec t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \bullet (1 / \\surdt)\nI. e^t cos t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \\cdot t^2\nJ. sin t, (1 / \\surd\\pi) \\cdot e^{{-t^2}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transforms:\n\n1.  **For (a) $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{2s}{(s^2+1)^2}\\right\\}$**: Using the property $\\mathcal{L}\\{t f(t)\\} = -F'(s)$, we know $\\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin t\\} = \\frac{1}{s^2+1}$. Differentiating $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s^2+1}$ gives $F'(s) = \\frac{-2s}{(s^2+1)^2}$, so $\\mathcal{L}\\{t \\sin t\\} = - \\left(\\frac{-2s}{(s^2+1)^2}\\right) = \\frac{2s}{(s^2+1)^2}$. Thus, the inverse is **$t \\sin t$**.\n2.  **For (b) $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{s}}\\right\\}$**: Using the formula $\\mathcal{L}\\{t^n\\} = \\frac{\\Gamma(n+1)}{s^{n+1}}$, let $n = -1/2$. Then $\\mathcal{L}\\{t^{-1/2}\\} = \\frac{\\Gamma(1/2)}{s^{1/2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}}{\\sqrt{s}}$, which implies $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{s}}\\right\\} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}$.\n\nComparing these results to the given options, Option A matches both results.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
