    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10712",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Obtain the time function corresponding to F(s) = [(s^2 + 3s + 1) / {{(s + 1)^3 (s + 2)^2}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. F(t) = - (3/2) t^2e^-t + 5te^-t - 6e^-t + (2/3)te^-2t + 3e^-2t\nB. F(t) = (1/3) t^2e^-t - te^-t + e^-t - (2/3)te^-2t - 3e^-2t\nC. F(t) = e^-t - 2te^-t + (1/2) t^2e^-t - e^-2t + (1/2)te^-2t\nD. F(t) = - (1/2) t^2e^-t + 3te^-t - 4e^-t + te^-2t + 4e^-2t\nE. F(t) = - (1/2) t^2e^-t + 3te^-t - 4e^-t - te^-2t - 4e^-2t\nF. F(t) = - (1/2) t^2e^-t - 3te^-t + 4e^-t - te^-2t + 4e^-2t\nG. F(t) = - t^2e^-t + 4te^-t - 5e^-t + 2te^-2t + 5e^-2t\nH. F(t) = (1/2) t^2e^-t + 3te^-t + 4e^-t + te^-2t + 4e^-2t\nI. F(t) = (1/2) t^2e^-t - 3te^-t + 4e^-t - (3/2)te^-2t - 6e^-2t\nJ. F(t) = - (1/4) t^2e^-t + 2te^-t - 3e^-t + (1/2)te^-2t + 2e^-2t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s) = \\frac{s^2 + 3s + 1}{(s + 1)^3 (s + 2)^2}$, we use partial fraction decomposition:\n$F(s) = \\frac{A}{(s+1)^3} + \\frac{B}{(s+1)^2} + \\frac{C}{s+1} + \\frac{D}{(s+2)^2} + \\frac{E}{s+2}$.\nSolving for the coefficients, we obtain $A = (-1)^2 + 3(-1) + 1 = -1$, $D = \\frac{(-2)^2 + 3(-2) + 1}{(-2+1)^3} = \\frac{-1}{-1} = 1$, and subsequently determine the remaining coefficients to match the time-domain function, which results in $F(t) = -\\frac{1}{2}t^2e^{-t} + 3te^{-t} - 4e^{-t} + te^{-2t} + 4e^{-2t}$. This expression corresponds exactly to option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
