      "generated_answer": "To find $f(t)$, we perform partial fraction expansion on $F(s) = \\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{(s + 1)(s + 3)}$. Since the degree of the numerator equals the degree of the denominator ($s^2 + 4s + 3$), we use long division to get $F(s) = 2 + \\frac{5s + 11}{(s + 1)(s + 3)}$. Expanding the remainder into partial fractions $\\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s+3}$ yields $A=3$ and $B=2$, resulting in $F(s) = 2 + \\frac{3}{s+1} + \\frac{2}{s+3}$. Taking the inverse Laplace transform gives $f(t) = 2\\delta(t) + (3e^{-t} + 2e^{-3t})u(t)$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
