    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10014",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Findcurlaat the point (1, - 2, 1) fora= x^2y^2i+ 2xyzj+ z^2k(1)\n\nOptions: \nA. (4, 4, 0)\nB. (-2, 0, 0)\nC. (0, 0, 4)\nD. (4, 0, 0)\nE. (2, 0, 0)\nF. (6, 0, 0)\nG. (0, -4, 0)\nH. (0, 2, 0)\nI. (2, 4, 2)\nJ. (0, 4, 0)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the curl of the vector field $\\mathbf{a} = x^2y^2\\mathbf{i} + 2xyz\\mathbf{j} + z^2\\mathbf{k}$, we calculate the determinant of the curl matrix:\n$\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\left( \\frac{\\partial (z^2)}{\\partial y} - \\frac{\\partial (2xyz)}{\\partial z} \\right)\\mathbf{i} - \\left( \\frac{\\partial (z^2)}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial (x^2y^2)}{\\partial z} \\right)\\mathbf{j} + \\left( \\frac{\\partial (2xyz)}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial (x^2y^2)}{\\partial y} \\right)\\mathbf{k}$.\nEvaluating the partial derivatives, we get $(0 - 2xy)\\mathbf{i} - (0 - 0)\\mathbf{j} + (2yz - 2x^2y)\\mathbf{k}$. Substituting the point $(1, -2, 1)$ results in $(-2(1)(-2))\\mathbf{i} + 0\\mathbf{j} + (2(-2)(1) - 2(1^2)(-2))\\mathbf{k} = 4\\mathbf{i} + 0\\mathbf{j} + 0\\mathbf{k}$, which is $(4, 0, 0)$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
