      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform $L^{-1} \\{ \\frac{1}{(s-1)^2} \\}$ using the convolution theorem, we can consider the function as the product of $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s-1}$ and $G(s) = \\frac{1}{s-1}$. Since $L^{-1} \\{ \\frac{1}{s-1} \\} = e^t$, the convolution is given by $\\int_0^t e^\\tau e^{t-\\tau} d\\tau = \\int_0^t e^t d\\tau$. Evaluating this integral yields $e^t [\\tau]_0^t = t e^t$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
