    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10160",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The plates of a parallel-plate capacitor are separated by a dielectric whose relative permittivity varies continuously with thickness as follows \\epsilon_r= [1 / {{1 - {{x^2 / (3d^2)}}] Compute the capacitance.\n\nOptions: \nA. (7/5) {{(\\epsilon_va) / (2d)}} Farad\nB. (9/8) {{(\\epsilon_va) + d}} Farad\nC. (8/9) {{(\\epsilon_va) \\cdot d}} Farad\nD. (1/2) {{(\\epsilon_va) \\cdot d}} Farad\nE. (3/2) {{(\\epsilon_va) / d}} Farad\nF. (8/9) {{(\\epsilon_va) / d}} Farad\nG. (9/8) {{(\\epsilon_va) \\cdot d}} Farad\nH. (5/7) {{(\\epsilon_va) / (d^2)}} Farad\nI. (9/8) {{(\\epsilon_va) / d}} Farad\nJ. (2/3) {{(\\epsilon_va) / d}} Farad\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the capacitance of a parallel-plate capacitor with a varying dielectric, we treat it as an infinite series of infinitesimal capacitors $dC$. The total capacitance $C$ is given by the reciprocal of the integral of the reciprocal of $dC$:\n$\\frac{1}{C} = \\int_{0}^{d} \\frac{dx}{\\epsilon_0 \\epsilon_r A} = \\int_{0}^{d} \\frac{1 - \\frac{x^2}{3d^2}}{\\epsilon_0 A} dx = \\frac{1}{\\epsilon_0 A} \\left[ x - \\frac{x^3}{9d^2} \\right]_0^d = \\frac{1}{\\epsilon_0 A} \\left( d - \\frac{d}{9} \\right) = \\frac{8d}{9\\epsilon_0 A}$.\nTaking the reciprocal, we get $C = \\frac{9\\epsilon_0 A}{8d}$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
