    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The function $g(t)$ can be rewritten using the unit step function $u(t-4)$ as $g(t) = (t-4)^2 u(t-4)$. According to the second shifting theorem of Laplace transforms, $\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\} = e^{-as}F(s)$, where $F(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\{f(t)\\}$. Given $f(t-4) = (t-4)^2$, we have $f(t) = t^2$, and since $\\mathcal{L}\\{t^2\\} = \\frac{2}{s^3}$, the transform is $e^{-4s} \\cdot \\frac{2}{s^3}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
