    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluatedivuat the point (- 1, 1, 2) foru= x^2i+e^xyj+ xyzk(1)\n\nOptions: \nA. - 3 - e^1\nB. - 2 - e^-1\nC. 2 + e^-1\nD. - 3 - e^-1\nE. -3 + e^1\nF. -4 + e^-1\nG. -1 + e^1\nH. -1 - e^-1\nI. - 3 + e^-1\nJ. -2 + e^1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the divergence of the vector field $\\mathbf{u} = x^2\\mathbf{i} + e^{xy}\\mathbf{j} + xyz\\mathbf{k}$, we calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(e^{xy}) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(xyz)$.\n1. $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2) = 2x$\n2. $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(e^{xy}) = xe^{xy}$\n3. $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(xyz) = xy$\n\nEvaluating $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 2x + xe^{xy} + xy$ at the point $(-1, 1, 2)$:\n$2(-1) + (-1)e^{(-1)(1)} + (-1)(1) = -2 - e^{-1} - 1 = -3 - e^{-1}$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
