    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10812",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A random variable R has a Rayleigh density f(r) = (r / \\alpha^2)e[{{-(r)2}} / {{2(\\alpha)2}}],0 \\leq r \\leq \\infty and = 0,r < 0 Determine the following: (a) the expected value or R, E [R] (b) the expected value of R^2, E [R^2] and (c) the variance \\sigma^2 of R\n\nOptions: \nA. E[R] = \\sqrt{{\\pi}}\\alpha/2, E[R^2] = \\pi\\alpha^2/2, \\sigma_r^2 = (\\pi - 3)\\alpha^2/2\nB. E[R] = 2\u0007lpha^2, E[R^2] = [\\surd(\\pi / 2)] \bullet \u0007lpha, \\sigma_r^2 = \u0007lpha^2(0.43)\nC. E[R] = \\alpha(1 - e^{{-1/2}}), E[R^2] = \\alpha^2, \\sigma_r^2 = \\alpha^2(e - 2)\nD. E[R] = \u0007lpha^2(0.43), E[R^2] = [\\surd(\\pi / 2)] \bullet \u0007lpha, \\sigma_r^2 = 2\u0007lpha^2\nE. E[R] = \\alpha\\sqrt{{e}}, E[R^2] = \\alpha^2\\ln(2), \\sigma_r^2 = \\alpha^2(2 - e/\\pi)\nF. E[R] = [\\surd(\\pi / 2)] \bullet \u0007lpha, E[R^2] = 2\u0007lpha^2, \\sigma_r^2 = \u0007lpha^2(0.43)\nG. E[R] = [\\surd(\\pi / 2)] \bullet \u0007lpha, E[R^2] = \u0007lpha^2(0.43), \\sigma_r^2 = 2\u0007lpha^2\nH. E[R] = \\alpha^2, E[R^2] = (2/3)\\alpha^2, \\sigma_r^2 = (4 - \\pi)\\alpha^2/2\nI. E[R] = \\alpha/\\sqrt{{2}}, E[R^2] = \\alpha^2, \\sigma_r^2 = \\alpha^2(\\pi - 2)/2\nJ. E[R] = \\alpha\\sqrt{{2/\\pi}}, E[R^2] = 3\\alpha^2/2, \\sigma_r^2 = \\alpha^2(1 - 2/\\pi)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For a Rayleigh distribution with parameter $\\alpha$, the expected values and variance are calculated as follows:\n(a) $E[R] = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\frac{r^2}{\\alpha^2} e^{-r^2/2\\alpha^2} dr = \\alpha \\sqrt{\\pi/2} \\approx 1.253\\alpha$.\n(b) $E[R^2] = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\frac{r^3}{\\alpha^2} e^{-r^2/2\\alpha^2} dr = 2\\alpha^2$.\n(c) $\\sigma_R^2 = E[R^2] - (E[R])^2 = 2\\alpha^2 - \\frac{\\pi\\alpha^2}{2} = \\alpha^2(2 - \\pi/2) \\approx 0.429\\alpha^2$.\n\nComparing these results to the options provided, Option F matches these derivations.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
