    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the duty cycle ($D$) for a step-up chopper (boost converter), we use the formula for the output voltage: $V_o = \\frac{V_{in}}{1 - D}$. \n\nRearranging the formula to solve for $D$:\n$1 - D = \\frac{V_{in}}{V_o} \\implies 1 - D = \\frac{110}{150} \\implies 1 - D \\approx 0.7333$\n$D = 1 - 0.7333 = 0.2667$, which rounds to approximately 0.27.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
