    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10912",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find y [n] such that y [n] - (5/6)y [n - 1] + (1/6)y [n - 2] = 3^n and y [- 1] = y [- 2] = 0, using the sum of the steady-state and homogene-ous solutions.\n\nOptions: \nA. y [n] = (26/20) 3^n - (3/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n\nB. y [n] = (27/20) 2^n - (3/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n\nC. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (3/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n.\nD. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (3/4) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n\nE. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (2/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n.\nF. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n + (3/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n\nG. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (3/5) (1/2)^n - (1/4) (1/3)^n\nH. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (4/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n.\nI. y [n] = (27/20) 3^n - (1/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n.\nJ. y [n] = (27/19) 3^n - (3/5) (1/2)^n + (1/4) (1/3)^n\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the solution, we first identify the homogeneous solution $y_h[n] = c_1(1/2)^n + c_2(1/3)^n$. We then find the steady-state (particular) solution $y_p[n] = A(3^n)$ by substituting into the recurrence, yielding $A(3^n) - \\frac{5}{6}A(3^{n-1}) + \\frac{1}{6}A(3^{n-2}) = 3^n$, which simplifies to $A(1 - 5/18 + 1/54) = 1$, resulting in $A = 27/20$. Using the initial conditions $y[-1]=0$ and $y[-2]=0$ to solve for $c_1$ and $c_2$ leads to the coefficients $-3/5$ and $1/4$, respectively.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
