    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10530",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The inductance of linear time-varying inductor is given by L(t) = L_0(t +tanht) and the current through it is given by i (t) =cos\\omegat Find the voltage across this inductor.\n\nOptions: \nA. U(t) = L_0 (1 - tanht)cos\\omegat + \\omegaL_0 (t - sech^2t)sin\\omegat\nB. U(t) = L_0 (1 + sech^2t)cos\\omegat+ \\omegaL_0 (t +tanht)sin\\omegat\nC. U(t) = L_0 (1 + sech^2t)cos\\omegat- \\omegaL_0 (t +tanht)sin\\omegat\nD. U(t) = L_0 (1 - sech^2t)cos\\omegat- \\omegaL_0 (t +tanht)sin\\omegat\nE. U(t) = -L_0 (1 + sech^2t)sin\\omegat + \\omegaL_0 (t + tanht)cos\\omegat\nF. U(t) = L_0 (1 + tanht)cos\\omegat - \\omegaL_0 (t - sech^2t)sin\\omegat\nG. U(t) = L_0 (1 + tanht)sin\\omegat - \\omegaL_0 (t + sech^2t)cos\\omegat\nH. U(t) = L_0 (1 - sech^2t)sin\\omegat + \\omegaL_0 (t + tanht)cos\\omegat\nI. U(t) = L_0 (2 + tanht)cos\\omegat - \\omegaL_0 sech^2t sin\\omegat\nJ. U(t) = L_0 (1 + sech^2t)sin\\omegat- \\omegaL_0 (t +tanht)cos\\omegat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The voltage across a time-varying inductor is defined by the relation $v(t) = \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}[L(t)i(t)]$. Using the product rule, $v(t) = i(t)\\frac{dL(t)}{dt} + L(t)\\frac{di(t)}{dt}$.\n\nGiven $L(t) = L_0(t + \\tanh t)$ and $i(t) = \\cos \\omega t$:\n1. $\\frac{dL(t)}{dt} = L_0(1 + \\text{sech}^2 t)$\n2. $\\frac{di(t)}{dt} = -\\omega \\sin \\omega t$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula yields:\n$v(t) = \\cos \\omega t \\cdot [L_0(1 + \\text{sech}^2 t)] + [L_0(t + \\tanh t)] \\cdot (-\\omega \\sin \\omega t)$\n$v(t) = L_0(1 + \\text{sech}^2 t)\\cos \\omega t - \\omega L_0(t + \\tanh t)\\sin \\omega t$\n\n\\boxed{C}",
