    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Write the following integrodifferential equation in the state form. [(d^2v) / (dt^2)] + a [(dv) / (dt)] +bv+ C ^t\\int_0 v(t')dt' = sin t\n\nOptions: \nA. q̇_2 = cq_1 + bq_2 + aq_3 - sin t\nB. q̇_3 = - cq_1 - bq_2 - aq_3 +cost\nC. q̇_3 = - cq_1 - bq_2 + aq_3 - sin t\nD. q̇_3 = - cq_1 - bq_2 - aq_3 -cost\nE. q̇_3 = - cq_1 + bq_2 - aq_3 + sin t\nF. q̇_1 = cq_2 + bq_3 + aq_1 + sin t\nG. q̇_3 = cq_1 + bq_2 + aq_3 +cost\nH. q̇_3 = cq_1 - bq_2 + aq_3 - sin t\nI. q̇_1 = - cq_2 - bq_3 - aq_1 + sin t\nJ. q̇_2 = - cq_1 - bq_2 - aq_3 +cost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To convert the integrodifferential equation $\\frac{d^2v}{dt^2} + a\\frac{dv}{dt} + bv + c\\int_0^t v(t')dt' = \\sin t$ into state-space form, we define the state variables as $q_1 = \\int_0^t v(t')dt'$, $q_2 = v$, and $q_3 = \\frac{dv}{dt}$. This leads to the system of first-order equations: $\\dot{q}_1 = q_2$, $\\dot{q}_2 = q_3$, and $\\dot{q}_3 = -cq_1 - bq_2 - aq_3 + \\sin t$. Although the options contain minor typographical discrepancies regarding the trigonometric term ($\\sin t$ vs $\\cos t$), Option B is the closest structural match for the state derivative $\\dot{q}_3$ based on the standard transformation.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
