    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the short circuit level at the busbar, we first calculate the short circuit MVA of a single alternator using the formula: $\\text{SC MVA (single)} = \\frac{\\text{Rating}}{\\text{Reactance}} = \\frac{20 \\text{ MVA}}{0.16} = 125 \\text{ MVA}$. Since there are four identical alternators operating in parallel, the total short circuit level at the busbar is the sum of their individual contributions: $4 \\times 125 \\text{ MVA} = 500 \\text{ MVA}$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
