    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10590",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using the Euler-Maclaurin summation formula ^\\infty \\sum_n=a f(n) = _a\\int^\\infty f(x)dx + (1/2) f(a) - (1 / 12)f'(a) + {{1 / (720)}} f\"'(a) + ..., evaluate the rotational partition function at high temperatures.\n\nOptions: \nA. q_rot = [(\\sigma\\Theta_rot^2) / T]\nB. q_rot = [\\Theta_rot / (T\\sigma)]\nC. q_rot = [T * (\\sigma\\Theta_rot)]\nD. q_rot = [\\Theta_rot / T^2]\nE. q_rot = [\\sigma / (T\\Theta_rot)]\nF. q_rot = [T / (\\Theta_rot^2)]\nG. q_rot = [(\\sigma\\Theta_rot) / T]\nH. q_rot = [T / (\\sigma\\Theta_rot)]\nI. q_rot = [T / (\\Theta_rot)]\nJ. q_rot = [T^2 / (\\sigma\\Theta_rot^2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rotational partition function for a heteronuclear diatomic molecule at high temperature is given by the sum $q_{rot} = \\sum_{J=0}^{\\infty} (2J+1) e^{-J(J+1)\\Theta_{rot}/T}$. For a general diatomic molecule (including homonuclear), the symmetry number $\\sigma$ is introduced, and the sum is approximated using the Euler-Maclaurin formula as $q_{rot} \\approx \\frac{1}{\\sigma} \\int_0^\\infty (2J+1) e^{-J(J+1)\\Theta_{rot}/T} dJ$. Evaluating this integral yields $q_{rot} = \\frac{T}{\\sigma\\Theta_{rot}}$, which corresponds to option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
