    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The fatigue loading applied on a compression spring consists of a minimum load of 145 lbs. to a maximum load of 295 lbs. Design the spring wire diameter for a factor of safety, based on fatigue failure to be 1.4 and the spring is assumed to have a mean coil diameter of 0.95 in. Consider the spring to be made of hard-drawn wire.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.35 in.\nB. 0.20 in.\nC. 0.28 in.\nD. 0.30 in.\nE. 0.18 in.\nF. 0.22 in.\nG. 0.25 in.\nH. 0.40 in.\nI. 0.32 in.\nJ. 0.15 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
