    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10225",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using the definition of the partial derivative of the vector, find: 1)(\\partiala/ \\partialu) 2)(\\partiala/ \\partialv) 3)[(\\partial^2a) / (\\partialu\\partialv) where a= (u^2v, u +e^v, u + v^2)(1)\n\nOptions: \nA. (2uv, 1, 1), (u^2,e^v, 2v), (2u, 1, 0)\nB. (2u, e^v, 2v), (2uv, 0, 1), (0, 1, 2v)\nC. (2uv, 1, 1), (u^2,e^v, 2u), (2u, 0, 0)\nD. (uv, 1, 2u), (2uv, 0, e^v), (2, e^v, 0)\nE. (2u, 1, 2v), (uv, e^v, 1), (0, 0, 2)\nF. (2uv, 1, 0), (u^2,e^v, 2v), (2u, 0, 0)\nG. (u^2, 0, 1), (2uv, 1, e^v), (0, 2u, 0)\nH. (2uv, 1, 1), (u^2,e^v, 2v), (2u, 0, 0)\nI. (0, 1, 2v), (u^2, 1, 1), (2uv, e^v, 0)\nJ. (2uv, 0, 1), (u^2, 1, 2u), (2, 0, e^v)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the partial derivatives of the vector $\\mathbf{a} = (u^2v, u + e^v, u + v^2)$:\n\n1.  **Partial derivative with respect to $u$ ($\\partial\\mathbf{a}/\\partial u$):** Differentiating each component with respect to $u$ (treating $v$ as a constant) gives $(2uv, 1, 1)$.\n2.  **Partial derivative with respect to $v$ ($\\partial\\mathbf{a}/\\partial v$):** Differentiating each component with respect to $v$ (treating $u$ as a constant) gives $(u^2, e^v, 2v)$.\n3.  **Mixed partial derivative ($\\partial^2\\mathbf{a}/\\partial u\\partial v$):** Differentiating $(\\partial\\mathbf{a}/\\partial v)$ with respect to $u$ gives $(2u, 0, 0)$.\n\nMatching these results with the provided options:\n- $\\partial\\mathbf{a}/\\partial u = (2uv, 1, 1)$\n- $\\partial\\mathbf{a}/\\partial v = (u^2, e^v, 2v)$\n- $\\partial^2\\mathbf{a}/\\partial u\\partial v = (2u, 0, 0)$\n\nThis corresponds to Option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
