    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10921",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A test charge q C, moving with a velocityv= (i_x +i_y) m/sec, experiences no force in a region of electric and magnetic fields. If the magnetic flux density B= (i_x - 2i_z)Wb/m^2, findE.\n\nOptions: \nA. (i_z - 2i_y) volts/m\nB. (-i_x + i_y) volts/m\nC. (3i_x - i_y - 2i_z) volts/m\nD. (2ix - 2i_y +i_z) volts/m\nE. (i_x - 2i_z) volts/m\nF. (2i_x - i_y) volts/m\nG. (i_x +i_y) volts/m\nH. (2ix + 2i_y -i_z) volts/m\nI. (i_y + i_z) volts/m\nJ. (i_x + 2i_y + i_z) volts/m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The force on a charge moving through electric and magnetic fields is given by the Lorentz force equation: $\\mathbf{F} = q(\\mathbf{E} + \\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{B})$. For the charge to experience no force, we must have $\\mathbf{E} = -(\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{B})$.\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i}_x + \\mathbf{i}_y$ and $\\mathbf{B} = \\mathbf{i}_x - 2\\mathbf{i}_z$, the cross product is:\n$\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{B} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i}_x & \\mathbf{i}_y & \\mathbf{i}_z \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}_x(-2 - 0) - \\mathbf{i}_y(-2 - 0) + \\mathbf{i}_z(0 - 1) = -2\\mathbf{i}_x + 2\\mathbf{i}_y - \\mathbf{i}_z$.\nThus, $\\mathbf{E} = -(-2\\mathbf{i}_x + 2\\mathbf{i}_y - \\mathbf{i}_z) = 2\\mathbf{i}_x - 2\\mathbf{i}_y + \\mathbf{i}_z$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
