      "generated_answer": "To find the magnetic intensity $\\mathbf{H}$ in free space, we use Faraday's Law in differential form, $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{E} = -\\mu_0 \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{H}}{\\partial t}$. Given $\\mathbf{E} = \\hat{j} A \\cos \\omega (t - z/c)$, the curl $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{E}$ results in $\\hat{i} \\frac{\\partial E_y}{\\partial z} = \\hat{i} \\frac{A\\omega}{c} \\sin \\omega (t - z/c)$. Integrating with respect to time yields $\\mathbf{H} = \\hat{i} \\frac{A}{c\\mu_0} \\cos \\omega (t - z/c)$, which satisfies the orthogonal relationship between $\\mathbf{E}$, $\\mathbf{H}$, and the direction of propagation $+z$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
