    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the ABCD parameters \\vertV_1\\vert = \\vertAB\\vert\\vert V_2 \\vert \\vertI_1\\vert\\vertCD\\vert\\vert- I_2\\vert(1) for a two port network. Find the G parameters, \\vertI_1\\vert = \\vertg_11g_12\\vert\\vertV_1\\vert \\vertV_2\\vert\\vertg_21g_22\\vert\\vertI2\\vert(2) in terms of the ABCD parameters.\n\nOptions: \nA. g_11 = (C/D), g_22 = (A / C), g_21 = (D / A), g_12 = {{(DC - AB) / (D)}}, y_12 = [(\\DeltaT) / D]\nB. g_11 = (D/B), g_22 = (A / D), g_21 = (C / B), g_12 = {{(BC - DA) / (B)}}, y_12 = [(\\DeltaT) / D]\nC. g_11 = (D/C), g_22 = (D / B), g_21 = (D / A), g_12 = {{(BD - AC) / (A)}}, y_12 = [(- \\DeltaT) / D]\nD. g_11 = (B/C), g_22 = (D / B), g_21 = (1 / C), g_12 = {{(BD - AC) / (B)}}, y_12 = [(- \\DeltaT) / B]\nE. g_11 = (C/A), g_22 = (B / A), g_21 = (1 / A), g_12 = {{(CB - AD) / (A)}}, y_12 = [(- \\DeltaT) / A]\nF. g_11 = (A/B), g_22 = (C / D), g_21 = (B / D), g_12 = {{(AB - CD) / (D)}}, y_12 = [(- \\DeltaT) / C]\nG. g_11 = (D/A), g_22 = (C / B), g_21 = (B / A), g_12 = {{(CA - BD) / (C)}}, y_12 = [(\\DeltaT) / C]\nH. g_11 = (B/A), g_22 = (C / A), g_21 = (A / D), g_12 = {{(AD - CB) / (A)}}, y_12 = [(\\DeltaT) / A]\nI. g_11 = (A/C), g_22 = (A / B), g_21 = (A), g_12 = {{(AD - BC) / (A)}}, y_12 = [(\\DeltaT) / B]\nJ. g_11 = (B/D), g_22 = (C / A), g_21 = (D / C), g_12 = {{(DA - CB) / (D)}}, y_12 = [(- \\DeltaT) / D]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the $g$-parameters in terms of $ABCD$ parameters, we start with the $ABCD$ transmission equations:\n1) $V_1 = AV_2 - BI_2$\n2) $I_1 = CV_2 - DI_2$\n\nWe need to express $I_1$ and $V_2$ in terms of $V_1$ and $I_2$. From (1), $AV_2 = V_1 + BI_2$, which gives $V_2 = \\frac{1}{A}V_1 + \\frac{B}{A}I_2$. Substituting $V_2$ into (2), we get $I_1 = C(\\frac{1}{A}V_1 + \\frac{B}{A}I_2) - DI_2 = \\frac{C}{A}V_1 + \\frac{CB - AD}{A}I_2$.\n\nComparing these to the $g$-parameter equations ($I_1 = g_{11}V_1 + g_{12}I_2$ and $V_2 = g_{21}V_1 + g_{22}I_2$), we find $g_{11} = \\frac{C}{A}$, $g_{12} = \\frac{CB - AD}{A}$, $g_{21} = \\frac{1}{A}$, and $g_{22} = \\frac{B}{A}$. These values, along with the determinant relation $\\Delta T = AD - BC$, match option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
