    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10872",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An input signal v(t) =I\\delta(t) (impulse function) is passed through a filter having function (1 - e-j\\omega\\tau)/j\\omegawhere \\tau is the stretchedumpulsewidth. Determine the output of the filter.\n\nOptions: \nA. v_o(t) = I [δ(t) * e^(-t/τ)]\nB. v_o(t) = I [e^(-jωt) - u(t - τ)]\nC. v_o(t) = I [1 - e^(-jωτ)]\nD. v_o(t) = I [u(t) / (u(t) + u(t - τ))]\nE. v_o(t) = I [u(t) / u(t - \tau)]\nF. v_o(t) = I [u(t) + u(t - \tau)]\nG. v_o(t) = I [u(t) * u(t - \tau)]\nH. v_o(t) = I [u(t) - u(t - \tau)]\nI. v_o(t) = I [δ(t) - e^(-t/τ)]\nJ. v_o(t) = I [sin(ωt) * u(t - τ)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output of a filter in the frequency domain is given by $V_o(\\omega) = V(\\omega) \\cdot H(\\omega)$. Since the input is an impulse $v(t) = I\\delta(t)$, its Fourier transform is $V(\\omega) = I$, making the output's frequency response $V_o(\\omega) = I \\frac{1 - e^{-j\\omega\\tau}}{j\\omega}$. Using the inverse Fourier transform property where $\\mathcal{F}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{j\\omega}\\} = u(t)$ and the time-shifting property $\\mathcal{F}^{-1}\\{\\frac{e^{-j\\omega\\tau}}{j\\omega}\\} = u(t - \\tau)$, the output in the time domain is $v_o(t) = I[u(t) - u(t - \\tau)]$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
