  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10372",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 200 W, 240 V, 50 Hz, 4-pole, 1-ph induction motor runs on rated load with a slip of 0.05 p. u. , The parameters are: r_1 = 11.4 \\Omega, x_1 = 14.5 \\Omega, (1/2) r_2 = 11 6.9 \\Omega, (1/2) x_2 = 7.2 \\Omega, (1/2)x_m= 135 \\Omega; core and mechanical loss, 32 W. Estimate the full-load performance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.67 p. u.\nB. 0.75 p. u.\nC. 0.63 p. u.\nD. 0.48 p. u.\nE. 0.85 p. u.\nF. 0.76 p. u.\nG. 0.58 p. u.\nH. 0.70 p. u.\nI. 0.82 p. u.\nJ. 0.55 p. u.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the full-load efficiency, we evaluate the forward and backward impedances of the single-phase induction motor at a slip $s = 0.05$.\n\n1.  **Impedances:**\n    *   Forward impedance $Z_f = \\frac{jX_m(r_2/s + jx_2)}{r_2/s + jx_2 + jX_m} \\approx 62.8 + j55.2 \\, \\Omega$\n    *   Backward impedance $Z_b = \\frac{jX_m(r_2/(2-s) + jx_2)}{r_2/(2-s) + jx_2 + jX_m} \\approx 6.4 + j13.5 \\, \\Omega$\n    *   Total Impedance $Z_{total} = Z_1 + Z_f + Z_b = (11.4 + j14.5) + (62.8 + j55.2) + (6.4 + j13.5) \\approx 80.6 + j83.2 \\, \\Omega$\n2.  **Current and Power:**\n    *   Current $I = \\frac{V}{|Z_{total}|} = \\frac{240}{\\sqrt{80.6^2 + 83.2^2}} \\approx 2.07 \\, \\text{A}$\n    *   Power Input $P_{in} = V \\cdot I \\cdot \\cos(\\phi) = 240 \\cdot 2.07 \\cdot \\frac{80.6}{115.8} \\approx 345.6 \\, \\text{W}$\n    *   Air gap power $P_{ag} = I^2(R_f - R_b) = 2.07^2(62.8 - 6.4) \\approx 241.6 \\, \\text{W}$\n    *   Mechanical Power $P_{mech} = (1-s)P_{ag} = 0.95 \\cdot 241.6 \\approx 229.5 \\, \\text{W}$\n    *   Net Output $P_{out} = P_{mech} - P_{rotational} = 229.5 - 32 = 197.5 \\, \\text{W}$\n3.  **Efficiency:** $\\eta = \\frac{P_{out}}{P_{in}} = \\frac{197.5}{345.6} \\approx 0.571$. Comparing with the options, 0.58 p.u. is the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
