    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10848",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Medium 1 has k_1 = 1.5 and extends to the left of theyz plane. Medium 2 hask_2= 2.5 and extends to the right of the yzplane. E_1 = (x̂2 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ) Vm^-1 FindD_1,E_2, andD_2.\n\nOptions: \nA. E_1 = x̂_1 - \\^{{y}}_2 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂0.6 - \\^{{y}}2 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂1.5 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ1), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂1.5 - \\^{{y}}5 + ẑ1.25)\nB. E_1 = x̂_3 - \\^{{y}}_3 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.3 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂2 - \\^{{y}}4.5 + ẑ_1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂2 - \\^{{y}}7.5 + ẑ2.5)\nC. E_1 = x̂_3 - \\^{{y}}_4 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.8 - \\^{{y}}4 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂4.5 - \\^{{y}}6 + ẑ2.25), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂4.5 - \\^{{y}}10 + ẑ3)\nD. E_1 = x̂_2 - \\^{{y}}_3.5 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.4 - \\^{{y}}3.5 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}5.25 + ẑ1.75), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂4.2 - \\^{{y}}8.75 + ẑ3.5)\nE. E_1 = x̂_1 - \\^{{y}}_3 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.1 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂4 - \\^{{y}}4.5 + ẑ_1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂4 - \\^{{y}}7.5 + ẑ2.5)\nF. E_1 = x̂_2 - \\^{{y}}_2 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.2 - \\^{{y}}2 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}3.5 + ẑ_1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}6.5 + ẑ2.5)\nG. E_1 = x̂_1.5 - \\^{{y}}_3 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂2.25 - \\^{{y}}4.5 + ẑ1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂2.5 - \\^{{y}}7.5 + ẑ2)\nH. E_1 = x̂_2.5 - \\^{{y}}_2.5 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.5 - \\^{{y}}2.5 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂3.75 - \\^{{y}}3.75 + ẑ1.875), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂3.75 - \\^{{y}}6.25 + ẑ2.5)\nI. E_1 = x̂_2 - \\^{{y}}_3 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.2 - \\^{{y}}3 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}4.5 + ẑ_1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}7.5 + ẑ2.5)\nJ. E_1 = x̂_2 - \\^{{y}}_4 + ẑ, E_2 = x̂1.5 - \\^{{y}}4 + ẑ, D_1 =\\epsilon_0(x̂3 - \\^{{y}}6 + ẑ1.5), D_2 = \\epsilon_0(x̂4.5 - \\^{{y}}10 + ẑ2.5)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the correct values, we use the boundary conditions for the interface at the $yz$-plane ($x=0$):\n1. **Tangential components of $E$ are continuous**: $E_{1y} = E_{2y} = -3$ and $E_{1z} = E_{2z} = 1$.\n2. **Normal component of $D$ is continuous**: $D_{1x} = D_{2x}$. Since $D = \\epsilon_0 k E$, we have $\\epsilon_0 k_1 E_{1x} = \\epsilon_0 k_2 E_{2x}$.\n3. **Calculations**:\n   - $D_1 = \\epsilon_0 k_1 E_1 = \\epsilon_0 (1.5)(2\\hat{x} - 3\\hat{y} + \\hat{z}) = \\epsilon_0 (3\\hat{x} - 4.5\\hat{y} + 1.5\\hat{z})$.\n   - $E_{2x} = \\frac{k_1}{k_2} E_{1x} = \\frac{1.5}{2.5}(2) = 1.2$. Thus, $E_2 = 1.2\\hat{x} - 3\\hat{y} + \\hat{z}$.\n   - $D_2 = \\epsilon_0 k_2 E_2 = \\epsilon_0 (2.5)(1.2\\hat{x} - 3\\hat{y} + \\hat{z}) = \\epsilon_0 (3\\hat{x} - 7.5\\hat{y} + 2.5\\hat{z})$.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option I matches perfectly.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
