    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10465",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 7-hp motor takes 6.3 kilowatts at full load. What is its efficiency ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 75%\nB. 86%\nC. 95%\nD. 60%\nE. 80%\nF. 83%\nG. 65%\nH. 70%\nI. 78%\nJ. 90%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the efficiency, we first convert the output power from horsepower to kilowatts using the conversion factor $1 \\text{ hp} = 0.746 \\text{ kW}$, which gives $7 \\text{ hp} \\times 0.746 \\approx 5.222 \\text{ kW}$. Efficiency is calculated as $(\\text{Output Power} / \\text{Input Power}) \\times 100$, which is $(5.222 \\text{ kW} / 6.3 \\text{ kW}) \\times 100 \\approx 82.88\\%$. Rounding to the nearest whole number provided in the options, we get 83%.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
