    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10601",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gaseous hydrochloric acid dissociates in water as described bythe following chemical reaction : HCl(g) \\rightarrow H^+(aq) +Cl^-(aq) Using the following heats of formation, calculate \\DeltaH°_77°F for thereaction. Heats of formation @ 77°F HCl-\\DeltaH_f= - 87.54 Btu/mole H^+ -\\DeltaH_f= 0 Btu/mole Cl^- -\\DeltaH_f= - 158.8 Btu/mole\n\nOptions: \nA. 87.54 Btu\nB. -87.54 Btu\nC. 0 Btu\nD. 158.8 Btu\nE. 71.26 Btu\nF. -158.8 Btu\nG. 246.34 Btu\nH. - 71.26 Btu\nI. -246.34 Btu\nJ. -175.34 Btu\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
