    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the joint resistance ($R_p$) of resistors in parallel, use the formula $\\frac{1}{R_p} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3} + \\frac{1}{R_4} + \\frac{1}{R_5}$.\nSubstituting the values: $\\frac{1}{R_p} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30} = 0.1 + 0.0667 + 0.05 + 0.04 + 0.0333 = 0.29$.\nCalculating the reciprocal gives $R_p = \\frac{1}{0.29} \\approx 3.448$ ohms, which most closely matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
