    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10847",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the homogeneous solution to a differential equation for thevoltagev_C(t) across a (1 / 2)F capacitor in a series RLC circuitwhere R = 4\\Omega, L = 4H,i_L(0) = (1 / 4) A, andv_C(0) = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. e-(1/2)tcos(1t) at V\nB. e-(1/4)tsin (1 / 2) at V\nC. e-(1/2)tsin (1) at V\nD. e-(1/4)tcos(2t) at V\nE. e-(1/2)tsin (1 / 2) at V\nF. e-(1/4)tcos(1t) at V\nG. e-(1/2)tsin(2t) at V\nH. e-(1)tcos(1/2t) at V\nI. e-(1/4)tsin(1t) at V\nJ. e-(1/2)tcos (1 / 2) at V\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the homogeneous solution for a series RLC circuit, we first determine the characteristic parameters: the damping factor $\\alpha = R/(2L) = 4/(2 \\times 4) = 0.5$ and the undamped resonant frequency $\\omega_0 = 1/\\sqrt{LC} = 1/\\sqrt{4 \\times 0.5} = 1/\\sqrt{2} \\approx 0.707$. Since $\\alpha^2 (0.25) > \\omega_0^2 (0.5)$, the circuit is overdamped; however, reviewing the options suggests an underdamped form $e^{-\\alpha t} \\sin(\\omega_d t)$ or $e^{-\\alpha t} \\cos(\\omega_d t)$ was intended with different values. Calculating for $\\alpha = 0.5$ and the initial condition $v_C(0) = 0$, the solution must be of the form $Ae^{-\\alpha t}\\sin(\\omega_d t)$, and with $\\alpha = 1/2$ and $\\omega_d = \\sqrt{\\omega_0^2 - \\alpha^2}$ (or a related frequency based on the provided options), option E matches the form $e^{-(1/2)t}\\sin(1/2)t$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
