    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a steady, turbulent, constant property, two dimensional boundarylayer-type flow over a flat plate at zero angle of approach, the velocity profile is given by u = v(y/\\delta)^1^/7(1) where v = free stream velocity \\delta = boundary layer thickness andthe local skin friction coefficient is given by C_f= [\\tau / {{(1/2)\\rhoV^2}}] = 0.045(ѵ /\\rhoV)^1/4(2) where \\tau = local shear stress \\rho = density of the flowing fluid ѵ = kinematic viscosity Determine the local boundary layer thickness \\delta, as a functionof x, by substituting the given equations into the integralform of the momentum equation.\n\nOptions: \nA. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.37x)^2}}{{(Re_x)^{{1/5}}\\)\nB. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.37x)}}{{(Re_x)^{{1/3}}\\)\nC. \\delta= {{(0.37x) / (Re_x)^1^/6}}\nD. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.47x)}}{{(Re_x)^{{1/5}}\\)\nE. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.37x)}}{{Re_x}}\\)\nF. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.50x)}}{{(Re_x)^{{1/5}}\\)\nG. \\delta= {{(0.37x) / (Re_x)^1^/5}}\nH. \\delta= {{(0.37x) / (Re_x)^1^/4}}\nI. \\(\\delta= \\frac{{(0.30x)}}{{(Re_x)^{{1/7}}\\)\nJ. \\delta= {{(0.72x) / (Re_x)^1^/5}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the local boundary layer thickness $\\delta(x)$, we use the von Kármán momentum integral equation: $\\frac{\\tau}{\\rho V^2} = \\frac{d\\theta}{dx}$. For a $1/7$-power law velocity profile, the momentum thickness $\\theta$ is calculated as $\\theta = \\int_{0}^{\\delta} \\frac{u}{V}(1 - \\frac{u}{V}) dy = \\frac{7}{72}\\delta$. Substituting the given skin friction coefficient $C_f = \\frac{\\tau}{\\frac{1}{2}\\rho V^2} = 0.045(\\frac{\\nu}{V\\delta})^{1/4}$ into the differential equation and integrating with respect to $x$ (with $\\delta=0$ at $x=0$) yields the solution $\\delta = 0.37x(Re_x)^{-1/5}$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
