    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the required phasors, we use Kirchhoff's voltage law relationships ($V_{ab} = V_{ax} + V_{xb}$):\n\n(a) $V_{14} = V_{12} + V_{24} = 6\\angle30^\\circ + 6\\angle-60^\\circ = (5.196 + j3) + (3 - j5.196) = 8.196 - j2.196 = 8.485\\angle-15^\\circ$.\n(b) $V_{43} = V_{42} + V_{23} = -V_{24} + V_{23} = -6\\angle-60^\\circ + 2\\angle0^\\circ = (-3 + j5.196) + 2 = -1 + j5.196 = 5.29\\angle100.89^\\circ$.\n(c) $V_{35} = V_{32} + V_{21} + V_{15} = -2\\angle0^\\circ - 6\\angle30^\\circ + 4\\angle90^\\circ = -2 - (5.196 + j3) + j4 = -7.196 + j1 = 7.265\\angle172.09^\\circ$.\n\nComparing these results with the given options, Option B provides the closest matches for all three values.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
