    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10798",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The shaft of a centrifugal pump is supported by a 180° centralpartial journal bearing 3 in. in diameter and 6 in. long. The clearance between the shaft and the bearing is 0.003 in. For lubrication SAE 20 oil is used and the minimum oil thicknessis 0.002 in. The shaft rotates at 1000 rpm and the bearingis subjected to a pressure of 50 psi based on the projectedarea of the journal. Evaluate the average temperatureof the oil film and the power developed due to friction.\n\nOptions: \nA. 165°F, 0.088\nB. 145°F, 0.115\nC. 140°F, 0.120\nD. 150°F, 0.110\nE. 160°F, 0.0943\nF. 170°F, 0.085\nG. 175°F, 0.080\nH. 180°F, 0.105\nI. 190°F, 0.075\nJ. 155°F, 0.099\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve for the average temperature and power developed, we first determine the eccentricity ratio $\\epsilon$. Given the radial clearance $c = 0.003 \\text{ in.}$ and minimum film thickness $h_0 = 0.002 \\text{ in.}$, we have $h_0 = c(1 - \\epsilon)$, yielding $\\epsilon = 1 - (0.002/0.003) = 1/3$. Using Raimondi and Boyd charts for a $180^\\circ$ partial bearing with $L/D = 2$ and $\\epsilon = 0.33$, we find the corresponding Sommerfeld number and viscosity, which aligns with SAE 20 oil at approximately $160^\\circ \\text{F}$, and the friction factor calculations lead to a power loss of approximately $0.0943 \\text{ hp}$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
