    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Intestinal motility is a complex process, orchestrated by nerves, hormones and the presence of food in the stomach. Which statement about this process is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. At the start of a meal, the stomach increases its \"tone\" in order to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nB. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\nC. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for the absorption of nutrients after a meal has been consumed\nD. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for peristaltic movement of food after a meal has been consumed\nE. The release of glucagon after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nF. The stomach decreases its \"tone\" at the end of a meal to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nG. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, slows intestinal motility\nH. The release of insulin after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nI. The presence of partially digested protein and fiber in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G**.\n\nThe presence of partially digested fats and carbohydrates in the duodenum triggers the enterogastric reflex and the release of hormones like CCK and secretin, which inhibit gastric emptying and slow intestinal motility to allow for proper digestion and absorption. The Migrating Motor Complex (MMC) occurs only during fasting (not after a meal), and the stomach initially undergoes receptive relaxation (decreased tone) to accommodate food rather than increasing tone to expel it immediately.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
