    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This clinical scenario describes the **Potter sequence**, where a single primary underlying abnormality (renal agenesis) leads to a cascade of secondary effects (oligohydramnios, which in turn causes pulmonary hypoplasia and compression facies). A **sequence** is defined as a pattern of multiple anomalies derived from a single prior anomaly or mechanical factor. Therefore, the cascade from renal failure to lung underdevelopment is a classic example of this classification.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{F}.",
