    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the frequency of the offspring genotype AABBCC from a cross of AaBbCc × AaBbCc, we treat each gene locus independently according to the Law of Independent Assortment. For each heterozygous pair (e.g., Aa × Aa), the probability of producing a homozygous dominant offspring (AA) is 1/4. Therefore, the probability of the combined genotype AABBCC is (1/4) × (1/4) × (1/4) = 1/64.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
