      "generated_answer": "To find the acceleration, first convert the final velocity from km/h to m/s: $130 \\text{ km/h} \\div 3.6 \\approx 36.11 \\text{ m/s}$. Using the kinematic equation $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$ (where $u = 0$ and $s = 50 \\text{ m}$), we get $36.11^2 = 2 \\cdot a \\cdot 50$, which simplifies to $1304 \\approx 100a$. Solving for $a$ gives approximately $13.04 \\text{ m/s}^2$, which matches option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
