  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_5253",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On an average daily basis, the gross energy intake of a healthy woman is 9279 kJ, the energy content of her faeces and urine are 647 kJ and 318 kJ, respectively. Her average daily digestible energy intake and metabolisable energy intake would be, respectively,:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nB. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-318 kJ\nC. 9279-(318+647) kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nD. 9279+647 kJ and 9279-(318+647) kJ\nE. 9279+318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nF. 9279-647 kJ and 9279-(647+318) kJ\nG. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nH. 9279+318 kJ and 9279+647 kJ\nI. 9279 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nJ. 647 kJ and 318 kJ\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we use the standard physiological definitions of energy intake:\n1. **Digestible Energy (DE)** = Gross Energy (GE) - Faecal Energy.\n2. **Metabolisable Energy (ME)** = Digestible Energy - Urinary Energy (or GE - [Faecal + Urinary Energy]).\n\nGiven GE = 9279 kJ, Faeces = 647 kJ, and Urine = 318 kJ:\n- DE = 9279 - 647 kJ.\n- ME = 9279 - (647 + 318) kJ.\n\nComparing these calculations to the provided options, Option F matches these formulas.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
