      "generated_answer": "To perform a right lateral excursion of the mandible, the contralateral (left) lateral pterygoid and medial pterygoid muscles must contract to pull the left condyle forward and medially (translation). Simultaneously, the ipsilateral (right) temporalis and masseter muscles act to stabilize the right condyle as it rotates. Therefore, the left lateral pterygoid is the primary muscle responsible for initiating and executing the movement to the right.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
