    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of this finding is that the benefit was discovered during a post hoc analysis rather than being a pre-specified primary endpoint. When multiple subgroups are analyzed after a trial fails its primary objective, the probability of finding a statistically significant result purely by chance increases (the multiple comparisons problem). Therefore, since vaccine response among African Americans was not the primary outcome measure, the finding is hypothesis-generating rather than definitive.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
