    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The p53 protein primarily acts as a cell cycle checkpoint regulator that induces cell cycle arrest at the **G1** phase in response to DNA damage (such as that caused by radiation). When TP53 is mutated and inactive, cells fail to halt in G1 to repair damage or undergo apoptosis, allowing for the continued proliferation of damaged cells and tumor progression. Therefore, the defect in cell cycle arrest occurs in the G1 phase.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
