    "global index": "MedMCQA_419",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Square root of pq/n indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Standard error of mean\nB. Standard error of difference of means\nC. Standard error of proportions\nD. Standard error of difference in proportions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}\n\n**Explanation:**\nThe formula $\\sqrt{pq/n}$ is used to calculate the **Standard Error of Proportions** (where $p$ is the proportion of success, $q = 1-p$, and $n$ is the sample size). For the standard error of the difference in proportions, the formula would involve two different samples (e.g., $\\sqrt{p_1q_1/n_1 + p_2q_2/n_2}$). Standard error of the mean uses standard deviation ($\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}$) rather than proportions.",
