    "global index": "MedMCQA_1200",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Multifactorial Causation\" theory was given by\n\nOptions: \nA. McMohan Pugh\nB. Pettenkofer of Munich\nC. Winslow\nD. Robert Koch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The theory of \"Multifactorial Causation,\" which suggests that diseases (especially non-communicable ones) are caused by multiple interacting factors rather than a single agent, was proposed by **Pettenkofer of Munich**. While McMahon and Pugh are associated with the \"Web of Causation,\" Pettenkofer is credited with the initial multifactorial concept.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{B}.",
