    "global index": "MedMCQA_145",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transport of CO is diffusion limited because\n\nOptions: \nA. Binds avidly with Hb\nB. Partial pressure of CO is less\nC. CO is less absorbed in water\nD. Alveolar membrane is less permeable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Carbon monoxide (CO) is considered diffusion-limited because it binds to hemoglobin (Hb) with an affinity over 200 times greater than oxygen, preventing the partial pressure of CO in the pulmonary capillary blood from rising significantly. Since the partial pressure gradient between the alveoli and the blood remains high throughout the transit time, the amount of CO transferred is limited only by the diffusion properties of the membrane rather than blood flow. Therefore, its uptake is governed by its avid binding to hemoglobin.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
