    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measuring variation between two different units is done through\n\nOptions: \nA. Variance\nB. Standard deviation\nC. Coefficient of variation\nD. Range\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Measuring variation between two different units requires a relative measure of dispersion that is dimensionless. The **Coefficient of Variation** (CV) is calculated as $(\\text{Standard Deviation} / \\text{Mean}) \\times 100$, allowing for the comparison of datasets with different units or widely different means. Options A, B, and D are absolute measures of dispersion and remain expressed in the original units of the data.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{C}.",
