      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nThiopental has a very high lipid solubility, allowing it to cross the blood-brain barrier almost instantaneously to induce anesthesia. However, its short duration of action is due to **redistribution**, where the drug rapidly leaves the brain and enters highly perfused lean tissues (muscle), followed by slower accumulation in fat. While high lipid solubility (Option C) facilitates this movement, Option D specifically describes the mechanism of redistribution that terminates its clinical effect.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
