      "generated_answer": "To exclude a disease, a test with high **sensitivity** is required because a negative result in a highly sensitive test effectively rules out the condition (the \"SnNOut\" mnemonic: Sensitivity, Negative result, Rule out). High sensitivity ensures that there are very few false negatives, making it the ideal metric for screening and exclusion. In contrast, specificity is used to confirm a disease (SpPIn).\n\n\\boxed{D}",
