    "global index": "MedMCQA_1595",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Feed forward mechanism..\n\nOptions: \nA. Feeling thirsty while walking in hot temperature\nB. Shivering on exposure to cold temperature\nC. Salivation on smelling food\nD. Increase blood pressure during supine posture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**.\n\n**Explanation:**\nA feed-forward mechanism is an anticipatory response that prepares the body for a change before it actually occurs. Salivation upon smelling food is a classic example (the cephalic phase of digestion), where the body prepares for ingestion before food actually enters the mouth, unlike feedback mechanisms which respond after a stimulus has altered a physiological variable.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
