    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following gives the rate of drug absorption in plasma concentration graph?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tmax and Cmax\nB. Area under the curve\nC. Tmax alone\nD. Cmax alone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In a plasma concentration-time curve, the rate of drug absorption is primarily determined by $T_{max}$ (the time taken to reach peak concentration) and $C_{max}$ (the peak concentration reached). While $C_{max}$ is influenced by the extent of absorption, $T_{max}$ is a direct indicator of how quickly the drug enters the systemic circulation. Therefore, both parameters together provide the most comprehensive assessment of the absorption rate.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
