    "global index": "MedMCQA_2313",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The setting time of zinc phosphate may be retarded by?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase in the ratio of powder to liquid\nB. Diluting the liquid with water\nC. Increase the addition of powder to liquid\nD. Decrease the addition of powder to liquid\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nThe setting time of zinc phosphate cement can be retarded (slowed down) by decreasing the powder-to-liquid ratio, which provides more liquid to react with the powder and results in a slower reaction. Conversely, increasing the powder-to-liquid ratio, adding water, or mixing on a warm slab would accelerate the setting time. Using a chilled glass slab and adding powder in small increments are the standard clinical methods to increase working time.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
