    "global index": "MedMCQA_2178",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What should be the time of termination of pregnancy of a female with insulin dependent diabetes?\n\nOptions: \nA. 40 weeks\nB. 38 weeks\nC. 37 weeks\nD. 34 weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In current obstetric practice, for women with pre-gestational insulin-dependent diabetes that is well-controlled and without vascular complications, delivery is typically recommended between 39 weeks 0 days and 39 weeks 6 days; however, if there are complications or slightly less than optimal control, delivery is often recommended at **38 weeks**. Many clinical guidelines and standard textbooks (such as DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics) historically and frequently cite 38 weeks as the optimal balance between fetal maturity and the risk of stillbirth or macrosomia. Therefore, B is the most widely accepted answer in this testing context.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
