    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hormone Replacement therapy is not indicated in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hot flashes\nB. Prevention of CAD\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Vaginal atrophy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**.\n\nWhile Hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT) was once thought to be cardioprotective, major clinical trials (such as the Women's Health Initiative) demonstrated that it does not prevent Coronary Artery Disease (CAD) and may actually increase the risk of cardiovascular events in certain populations. Conversely, HRT is a well-established treatment for vasomotor symptoms like hot flashes, vaginal atrophy, and the prevention of osteoporosis.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
