      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nThe function described in option D (resisting displacement away from the basal seat) is the definition of **retention**, which is primarily provided by the retentive clasp arms engaging undercuts, not by guiding planes. Guiding planes are responsible for establishing a single path of placement, providing lateral stability, and ensuring the prosthesis moves without binding or straining the abutment teeth.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
