    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sequential arrangement question on JVP. Staing with \"a\" wave. A-First hea sound B-T wave C-R wave D-Rapid ejection phase\n\nOptions: \nA. A,B,C,D\nB. A,C,D,B\nC. C,A,D,B\nD. D,C,B,A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct sequence starting from the **'a' wave** of the Jugular Venous Pressure (JVP), we must correlate its timing with the cardiac cycle and ECG:\n1. The **'a' wave** (atrial contraction) occurs just after the P wave and is followed by the **R wave** (C) of the ECG.\n2. The **First heart sound** (A) occurs shortly after the R wave during isovolumetric contraction.\n3. This is followed by the **Rapid ejection phase** (D) of the ventricles.\n4. Finally, ventricular repolarization is represented by the **T wave** (B) on the ECG.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
