    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A properly designed rest on lingual surface of a canine is preferred to a rest on incisal surface because:\n\nOptions: \nA. Less Leverage is exerted against the tooth by Lingual rest\nB. Enamel is thicker on lingual surface\nC. Visibility and access is better on lingual surface\nD. The cingulum of canine produces a naturalsurface for recess\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nA lingual rest is preferred because it is placed closer to the horizontal axis of rotation of the tooth, thereby reducing the tipping forces (leverage) compared to an incisal rest. Additionally, lingual rests are more esthetically pleasing and less likely to interfere with occlusion. While the cingulum provides a natural area for preparation, the primary mechanical advantage is the reduction of unfavorable leverage.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
