      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**.\n\nClass II composite restorations require thorough polymerization at the deep gingival floor; curing from the occlusal aspect only leads to incomplete polymerization at the bottom of the box due to the distance and shadow effect of the tooth structure. This results in \"polymerization shrinkage\" away from the gingival margin or the presence of residual monomers, leading to microleakage and subsequent postoperative sensitivity. Options C and D are actually techniques used to *reduce* sensitivity and ensure better marginal adaptation.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
