    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following event has little or no significance?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mandibular incisor erupting before mandibular molar\nB. Mandibular canine erupting before mandibular premolar\nC. Mandibular 2nd premolar erupting before mandibular 2nd molar\nD. Maxillary premolar and canine erupting before maxillary 2nd molar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nIn the mandibular arch, the eruption of the first molar and the central incisor occurs at approximately the same time (around 6 years of age), and the sequence between them is highly variable and clinically insignificant. In contrast, the other sequences (B, C, and D) are critical for maintaining arch length and preventing crowding or impaction of the premolars and canines. Therefore, the mandibular incisor erupting before the mandibular molar has little to no clinical significance.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
