    "global index": "MedMCQA_1326",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the best index for burden of disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. Case fatality rate\nB. Morbidity data\nC. Dependency ratio\nD. Disability adjusted life years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **D**.\n\nThe Disability Adjusted Life Years (DALY) is the best index for burden of disease because it combines years of life lost due to premature mortality and years lived with disability into a single metric. Unlike morbidity or mortality data alone, DALYs provide a comprehensive measure of the total health loss within a population.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
