    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Based on the clinical presentation of hypertension (160/100 mm Hg) and tachycardia (120/min) in a patient likely suffering from an aortic dissection (implied by the CECT context), the immediate priority is heart rate and blood pressure control. **Beta blockers** are the first-line medical management to reduce the rate of rise of arterial pressure ($dP/dt$) and prevent further propagation of the dissection. Surgical repair is typically reserved for Type A dissections, but initial stabilization always begins with rate control.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
