      "generated_answer": "In an atrophic mandible with bone loss, the bone is unable to provide structural support, making \"load-sharing\" techniques (like semi-rigid fixation) prone to failure. The gold standard involves **bone grafting** to address the loss of volume and **load-bearing fixation** (using a heavy reconstruction plate) to take over the full mechanical stress of the mandible. This approach ensures stability and promotes successful integration of the graft.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
