      "generated_answer": "The study found that BRAF mutation status positively influenced progression-free survival (PFS) in patients treated with tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs), with a significant difference of 34.7 months versus 11.6 months. Although histology was the only independent prognostic factor in multivariate analysis, the molecular profile correlated with patient outcomes and treatment response. Therefore, molecular genotyping provides valuable clinical information for managing these patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
