      "generated_answer": "The study found that patients who switched from folic acid to a placebo were significantly more likely to discontinue the study early (46% vs. 21%) and experienced a higher incidence of side effects like nausea and neutropenia. While there were minor improvements in disease activity variables in the placebo group, they were not considered clinically significant compared to the increased toxicity. Therefore, the results suggest that continuing folic acid is beneficial for managing methotrexate toxicity in these patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
