    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In Neo-Riemannian theory, the **P (Parallel)** transformation maps a major triad to its parallel minor (and vice versa) by moving the third of the chord by a half step. In this case, the A major triad (A, C#, E) becomes the A minor triad (A, C, E) by shifting the C# down to C. Therefore, the P transformation is the correct operation for this change.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
