      "generated_answer": "To find a diminished sixth below **F#**, we first determine the sixth note name counting downwards: F# (1), E (2), D (3), C (4), B (5), **A** (6). \n\nA major sixth below F# is A natural (9 semitones), a minor sixth below F# is A# (8 semitones), and a **diminished sixth** below F# is **A double-sharp (A##)** (7 semitones). Therefore, the root note must be A double-sharp to create the required interval.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
