    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Based on the text provided, the specific social reason for the masks is not fully detailed, though it is framed as a cultural norm where **women try to attract men even when the future seems bleak**. The story notes that masked women are a common sight and that the masks, such as the girl's \"sleek black satin mask\" with \"black gauze covering the eyeholes,\" serve as a form of fashion or protection in a volatile society. The narrative suggests a world of gender-based tension where men (the \"rippers\") aggressively target women's clothing, and the masks may be part of a broader social concealment or \"attraction\" ritual.\n\n\\boxed{The text indicates that women wear masks and coverings as a societal norm to attract men in a grim future, while also serving as a form of concealment. The masks are part of a culture where men aggressively target women's fashion, as seen in the \"rippers\" who try to snag skirts. They provide a layer of anonymity and stylized mystery in a dangerous, vice-ridden environment.}",
